the distribution network.<br>
This standard defines the equipment, functional performance, and coordination principles applicable to protective<br>
devices installed at the point of interconnection (POI) of an export-capable DER site. It is issued by Standards<br>
Engineering under authority of the Director of Distribution Engineering and shall be applied to all in-scope<br>
projects at initial screening, detailed engineering review, construction, and commissioning.<br>
2. SCOPE<br>
This standard applies to all distribution-connected export-capable DER sites within the Alleniom Utilities service<br>
territory, including but not limited to:<br>
1. Commercial small-scale DER (500 kW – 1 MW nameplate).<br>
2. Medium-scale DER (1 MW – 5 MW nameplate).<br>
3. Any DER of any size that is capable, by facility design or operating configuration, of exporting real power to<br>
the distribution system through the point of common coupling.<br>
Sub-scope DER handled under the Simplified Small-Systems Process are outside the direct application of this<br>
standard; however, where such a facility is nonetheless configured for export, the protection principles of §4 shall<br>
apply as adapted by the Small-Systems review.<br>
Non-export configurations (facilities operated behind a reverse-power lockout with no export capability under any<br>
operating condition) are outside the scope of this standard and are addressed under separate protection<br>
guidance.<br>
3. REFERENCES<br>
The following documents are referenced in the application of this standard:<br>
 IEEE 1547 — Standard for Interconnection and Interoperability of Distributed Energy Resources with<br>
Associated Electric Power Systems Interfaces.<br>
 IEEE C37.230 — Guide for Protective Relay Applications to Distribution Lines.<br>
 IEEE C37.60 / IEC 62271-111 — Requirements for Overhead, Pad-Mounted, Dry-Vault, and Submersible<br>
Automatic Circuit Reclosers.<br>
 ANSI C57.13 — Requirements for Instrument Transformers.</p>
<hr>
<p>DPS-07 Rev 2  |  Distribution Protection Standard  |  Effective 09/15/2023 Page 2<br>
 Alleniom Utilities TCS-02 — Telemetry &amp; Communications Standard.<br>
 Alleniom Utilities ERP-9 — Engineering Referral Procedure.<br>
4. PROTECTION REQUIREMENTS<br>
4.1 General<br>
Every distribution-connected DER site subject to this standard shall be equipped with protective equipment<br>
sufficient to accomplish, at minimum, the following:<br>
(a) Isolate the DER from the distribution system upon loss of the utility source, before the operation of any utility<br>
reclosing sequence that would attempt to re-energize the affected circuit.<br>
(b) Isolate the DER from the distribution system upon detection of abnormal voltage or frequency conditions on<br>
the utility side of the point of interconnection, within the trip times required by the applicable interconnection<br>
standard.<br>
(c)Present the utility system operator with a visible, remotely operable, and lockable point of interruption<br>
between the DER and the distribution circuit at all times when the DER is connected.<br>
(d) Coordinate with upstream and downstream distribution protective devices such that a DER-side fault is<br>
cleared by DER-side devices and a utility-side fault is cleared by utility-side devices, without unnecessary<br>
tripping of either.<br>
4.2 Point-of-Interconnection Recloser Requirement<br>
Every export-capable in-scope DER site shall be equipped with a utility-owned point-of-interconnection<br>
(POI) recloser. No exceptions are specified.<br>
The POI recloser shall satisfy the following requirements:<br>
1. Ownership and control. The POI recloser and its associated control cabinet, communications interface,<br>
current and voltage transformers, and control power supply shall be owned, installed, maintained, and<br>
operated by Alleniom Utilities. The DER owner shall provide the physical site, the equipment pad, primary<br>
conductors to the recloser terminals, and any auxiliary services (grounding, station service, communications<br>
backhaul) as specified in the site''s construction package.<br>
2. Ratings. The recloser shall be rated for the maximum continuous current, momentary current, short-circuit<br>
interrupting current, and system voltage of the feeder or lateral to which it is connected, with margin per<br>
Distribution Protection Engineering''s feeder-specific settings sheet.<br>
3. Functional elements. At minimum, the recloser control shall implement the following ANSI device functions,<br>
with settings determined per site by Distribution Protection Engineering:<br>
— 50/51 phase and 50N/51N ground overcurrent (instantaneous and time),<br>
— 27/59 undervoltage and overvoltage,<br>
— 81U/81O underfrequency and overfrequency,<br>
— 25 synchronism check for closing into an energized system,<br>
— 32 directional power element, available for use as an export-limit enforcement or reverse-power<br>
backstop as directed by the site''s engineering determination,<br>
— 79 automatic reclosing, enabled or blocked per the coordination scheme in §5.<br>
4. Operability. The recloser shall be capable of local manual operation, local electrical operation from the<br>
control cabinet, and remote operation and monitoring via the utility SCADA system per TCS-02. Loss of<br>
communications shall not defeat local protection.<br>
Where a referenced external standard is revised, the revision in effect on the date of the site''s engineering<br>
determination shall govern, unless Standards Engineering directs otherwise in writing.</p>
<hr>
<p>DPS-07 Rev 2  |  Distribution Protection Standard  |  Effective 09/15/2023<br>
Page 3<br>
5. Visible break and lockout. The recloser shall provide, or be paired with, a visible-break disconnect<br>
operable by utility personnel, with provision for utility padlocking in the open position for the purpose of<br>
clearance holds.<br>
6. Location. The POI recloser shall be located on the utility side of the point of interconnection, at a location<br>
accessible to Alleniom Utilities crews 24 hours per day, 7 days per week, without transiting locked customer<br>
premises.<br>
4.3 DER-Side Protection<br>
DER-side protection (generator step-up transformer protection, inverter interface protection, plant collection<br>
protection, and any owner-installed disconnects) shall be provided by the DER owner, coordinated with the POI<br>
recloser settings, and reviewed by Alleniom Utilities Distribution Protection Engineering prior to commissioning.<br>
DER-side protection does not substitute for the POI recloser required under §4.2.<br>
4.4 Grounding<br>
The DER interconnection transformer grounding configuration shall be determined per site to be compatible with<br>
the grounding of the connected distribution circuit, in accordance with Distribution Protection Engineering''s<br>
grounding practice memorandum for the affected feeder class.<br>
4.5 Anti-Islanding<br>
The DER shall be equipped with anti-islanding protection meeting the trip times and non-detection zone<br>
requirements of the applicable interconnection standard. Passive schemes based solely on utility-side voltage<br>
and frequency measurement are permitted only where the site''s system impact study demonstrates the passive<br>
scheme''s detection performance for the range of expected islanding conditions on the connected feeder;<br>
otherwise an active or communications-assisted scheme shall be provided.<br>
5. COORDINATION REQUIREMENTS<br>
5.1 Coordination with Feeder Reclosing<br>
The POI recloser shall be coordinated with the upstream feeder recloser and any mid-line reclosers such that:<br>
(a) The POI recloser opens on loss of the utility source before the first reclose attempt of any upstream<br>
recloser.<br>
(b) The POI recloser remains open and locked out until the utility source has been restored, verified stable per<br>
the site''s synchronism-check settings, and the utility system operator has authorized reconnection per the<br>
site''s operating procedure.<br>
(c) Coordination time-current characteristics shall be documented in the site''s protection coordination study<br>
prior to energization.<br>
5.2 Coordination with DER-Side Protection<br>
DER-side protective devices shall clear DER-side faults without operation of the POI recloser to the extent<br>
reasonably practicable. Where a DER-side fault is not cleared by DER-side devices within the allowable time, the<br>
POI recloser shall trip as backup protection.<br>
5.3 Direct Transfer Trip<br>
Direct transfer trip (DTT) shall be applied at any site where the system impact study identifies an unacceptable<br>
non-detection zone for anti-islanding, or where the connected feeder configuration requires supervised opening<br>
of the POI recloser on operation of an upstream device. Where DTT is applied, the associated communications<br>
channel shall meet the availability and monitoring requirements of TCS-02.<br>
5.4 Reclosing Blocking<br>
Automatic reclosing on the upstream feeder recloser may be blocked, delayed, or supervised at sites where the<br>
DER contribution to fault current, the DER anti-islanding characteristic, or the customer load composition on the</p>
<hr>
<p>DPS-07 Rev 2  |  Distribution Protection Standard  |  Effective 09/15/2023 Page 4<br>
affected feeder warrants such a change. The determination shall be made per site by Distribution Protection<br>
5.5 Settings Governance<br>
All protection settings for the POI recloser, and any changes to upstream feeder recloser settings driven by the<br>
DER interconnection, shall be issued in writing by Distribution Protection Engineering and shall not be altered in<br>
the field without a written revision order.<br>
6. TESTING<br>
6.1 Factory Acceptance<br>
The POI recloser and its control shall be subjected to factory acceptance testing per the manufacturer''s standard<br>
test protocol and per IEEE C37.60 / IEC 62271-111, with test records delivered to Alleniom Utilities prior to<br>
shipment.<br>
6.2 Site Acceptance<br>
Prior to placing the DER site in service, the following site acceptance activities shall be performed and witnessed<br>
by Alleniom Utilities:<br>
1. Insulation resistance and dielectric withstand testing of primary and secondary circuits.<br>
2. Current transformer and voltage transformer ratio, polarity, and burden verification.<br>
3. Functional testing of each enabled ANSI device function against its issued setting, including pickup, timing,<br>
and reset.<br>
4. End-to-end trip testing from each protection element through the recloser interrupter.<br>
5. Verification of local and remote (SCADA) control, status, and metering per TCS-02.<br>
6. Verification of synchronism check and reclose-block logic.<br>
7. Verification of visible-break disconnect operation and lockout provisions.<br>
6.3 Commissioning and Cutover<br>
Cutover of the DER site to the distribution system shall not proceed until all §6.2 activities are complete and<br>
accepted in writing by Alleniom Utilities. The site''s initial parallel operation shall be observed by the utility system<br>
operator with the POI recloser under active SCADA supervision.<br>
6.4 Periodic Testing<br>
The POI recloser shall be included in the utility''s periodic recloser maintenance program. DER-side protective<br>
devices shall be tested by the DER owner on a schedule not to exceed that of comparable utility-owned<br>
equipment, with test records made available to Alleniom Utilities on request.<br>
6.5 Post-Event Testing<br>
Following any operation of the POI recloser attributable to a system disturbance, a DER-side event, or a<br>
mis-operation, Distribution Protection Engineering shall review the event records and direct such retesting or<br>
resetting as it determines appropriate before the site is returned to service.<br>
End of DPS-07 Rev 2 — Distribution Protection Standard. Distribution: Alleniom Standards Engineering master file;<br>
Distribution Protection Engineering; Distribution Operations; DER Program Office; APUC filing (informational).<br>
Engineering and recorded in the site''s interconnection file.</p>', '[]', 'markdown', '2026-11-19T12:07:38.055842+00:00', '2026-11-19T12:07:38.055842+00:00', 'markdown', 'en', 9, 9, '{}');
