referred question shall proceed in parallel.<br>
The per-site engineering determination is issued in writing on Form ER-11 by Distribution Protection<br>
Engineering, is signed by the responsible engineer and countersigned by the Manager, Distribution<br>
Protection Engineering, and is filed with the application record. The determination is binding for the<br>
referred site and does not create a general rule across the program; a subsequent site presenting a similar<br>
question is referred and determined on its own facts.<br>
Where the site''s protection arrangement, as determined under this section, differs from the tabular default<br>
of DIS-01 §5 Table 5-1, the engineering determination on Form ER-11 supplements the site''s<br>
protective-equipment scoping and is provided to the DER Program Office and to the contracts desk for<br>
incorporation into the interconnection service agreement.<br>
Where the referral resolves a recurring pattern that Standards Engineering considers appropriate to reflect<br>
in a future revision of a standard, the determinations are logged and reviewed as provided in §5.</p>
<hr>
<p>§4 TIMELINES<br>
Timelines below run from the date on which Interconnection Studies transmits the completed Form ER-11<br>
to Distribution Protection Engineering. Business days exclude weekends and federal holidays.<br>
Referral class<br>
Description<br>
Determination due<br>
