Engineering review.<br>
30 business days<br>
Classification is made by the Manager, Distribution Protection Engineering, on receipt of Form ER-11.<br>
Where the reviewer requests reclassification, the request is decided in writing within two business days.<br>
Extensions to the timelines above are permitted only in writing, are issued by the Manager, Distribution<br>
Protection Engineering, and are copied to the DER Program Manager and Regulatory Affairs. Applications<br>
shall not be held in queue pending revision of a standard where this procedure provides a determination<br>
path; extensions do not authorize a screening hold outside this procedure.<br>
§5 DOCUMENTATION<br>
The completed Form ER-11, the engineering determination, and any supporting studies are filed with the<br>
application record retained by Interconnection Studies for the retention period established by Regulatory<br>
Affairs. A copy of the completed Form ER-11 is filed in the Standards Engineering ERP-9 register of<br>
per-site determinations.<br>
The ERP-9 register records, at minimum: the referral number, the receipt date, the Project ID, the site type<br>
and feeder, the standards documents at issue, the assigned engineer, the determination date, and a short<br>
summary of the determination. The register is reviewed by Standards Engineering quarterly for recurring<br>
patterns; where a pattern warrants a standards revision proposal, Standards Engineering initiates that<br>
revision separately from, and in parallel with, ongoing per-site determinations under this procedure. A<br>
pending revision proposal does not stay determinations issued under this procedure and does not<br>
authorize a screening hold on affected applications.<br>
Determinations issued under ERP-9 are cited in the interconnection service agreement (ISA) drafted for<br>
the affected site by reference to the ER-11 referral number and determination date. Modifications to the<br>
site''s protection arrangement subsequent to ISA execution are handled under the change-order provisions<br>
of the executed ISA, subject to DIS-01 §7 where capacity or POI is affected.</p>
