EXHIBIT B — FACILITY AND INTERCONNECTION FACILITIES<br>
B.1 Generating equipment. Five Vexlar VX-140C inverters, INV-C1 to INV-C5, 140 kW (ac) each at 480 V, three-phase, one on each of canopies C1 to C5; 700 kW (ac) in all. The inverters provide the interconnection protective functions by their certified functions (DIS Table 5-1, Category 2) and operate at the IEEE 1547-2018 Category III default settings and constant power factor 1.00 unless the Company directs otherwise in writing.<br>
B.2 Interconnection Customer''s interconnection facilities. Inverter ac disconnects AD-C1 to AD-C5, one beside each inverter; PV switchboard SWBD-PV with five 225 A inverter breakers and a 1,200 A main breaker; step-up transformer T-1, 750 kVA, 13.2 kV grounded wye to 480Y/277 V; primary switch PSW-1 with current-limiting fuses; the 13.2 kV primary conductors from PSW-1 to the Point of Interconnection.<br>
B.3 Monitoring. The PV monitoring cabinet DAS-1 is the Interconnection Customer''s own monitoring and is not part of the Company''s telemetry.</p>', '[]', 'markdown', '2026-11-19T12:07:38.055842+00:00', '2026-11-19T12:07:38.055842+00:00', 'markdown', 'en', 5, 5, '{}');
