382C ''today'':438C,483C ''toler'':363C ''topolog'':194C ''tracker'':182C ''tue'':33C ''turnaround'':495C ''unblock'':476C ''unchang'':176C,248C,405C ''understand'':455C ''updat'':46C,88C,150C,290C ''us'':379C ''vellanki'':50C ''via'':17B,118C ''viabl'':377C ''visibl'':454C ''week'':337C ''within'':224C ''work'':262C ''workabl'':104C ''would'':429C,433C ''write'':80C', '2025 07 08 amendment request from corey lindqvist corey.lindqvist hailbouysolar.com to der.program alleniom.com date tue 08 jul 2025 09 14 22 0500 subject harkwell ridge isa capacity update request cc meera vellanki meera.vellanki alleniom.com program office following execution of the interconnection service agreement on 07 03 2025 for harkwell ridge solar application pxa 2024 0117 at 2.2 mw hailbouy solar is writing to request that the executed isa be updated to reflect nameplate export capacity of 2.8 mw our preference and we believe the only workable path given the project construction and financing calendar is to effect this change via short addendum to the executed isa background and rationale the isa as executed on 07 03 2025 fixes capacity at 2.2 mw on feeder aln 042 post execution offtake refinements and updated production modeling from our epc support revised design point of 2.8 mw at the same point of interconnection the equipment schedule and site plan are unchanged in configuration the single axis tracker layout module count per string row geometry inverter locations mv collection topology poi structure and interconnection facilities scope on file with the der program office are all as approved the delta is firmware level export setting and dc ac ratio adjustment within the equipment already listed in the original application and reflected in the executed interconnection service agreement because the physical configuration and poi are unchanged no re study should be needed the prior system impact and facilities study work performed under pxa 2024 0117 remains the applicable technical basis and short capacity only addendum executed against the existing isa is the appropriate instrument to memorialize the update requested action please prepare an addendum to isa harkwell ridge revising the article nameplate export capacity from 2.2 mw to 2.8 mw with all other terms of the executed isa to remain in full force and effect please route the addendum for countersignature by end of week 07 11 2025 our construction mobilization sequence epc commitment schedule and tax equity funding milestones are built around the 07 03 2025 execution and cannot tolerate slippage any process that reopens the study queue on this project is not viable for us on this timeline if the program office needs supplemental technical memo from our engineer of record confirming that the equipment schedule and site plan are unchanged in configuration we can have that in your hands by close of business 07 09 2025 please advise by return email if this would expedite the addendum would appreciate confirmation of receipt today and target date for the addendum draft meera copying you directly so interconnection studies has visibility understand the addendum sits with the contracts desk but if there is anything on the studies side that needs signoff to unblock the drafting please let me know today and we will accommodate given the timing sensitivity we consider expedited turnaround essential and are prepared to make our team available for same day call at alleniom convenience regards corey lindqvist project director hailbouy solar 2200 ridge point road suite 400 halston alleron 03ha 612 817 0554 corey.lindqvist hailbouysolar.com');
