58C,812C,827C,854C,870C,963C,1086C,1300C,1318C,1372C ''state'':91C,596C ''status'':953C ''studi'':211C,229C ''subject'':1234C ''successor'':666C,727C,826C,848C,1371C ''suffici'':350C ''suit'':119C ''supersed'':473C,664C,729C,778C,850C ''surviv'':691C ''system'':194C,207C,327C,445C,1015C ''take'':859C ''tap'':561C ''tariff'':257C,382C,807C,892C,1083C,1134C,1184C,1214C,1269C ''tcs'':753C,926C,1040C ''technic'':205C ''technolog'':532C,591C ''telemetri'':755C,874C,922C,960C,993C,1022C,1027C,1069C ''term'':287C,305C,365C,588C,602C,607C,642C,662C,1089C,1276C,1306C,1335C ''termin'':657C,693C,942C ''test'':903C ''therefor'':329C ''therein'':1129C ''thereof'':731C ''thirti'':1152C,1207C ''three'':558C ''time'':710C,780C,782C,920C ''titl'':1422C,1440C ''togeth'':964C,1464C ''tracker'':174C,537C ''transit'':865C ''two'':635C,1450C ''typograph'':1325C ''undertak'':337C ''unit'':943C ''unless'':1160C ''upgrad'':1105C ''use'':1066C ''util'':22C,79C,84C,267C,939C,1021C,1415C,1480C ''valuabl'':345C ''veldmer'':27C,99C ''vice'':1423C ''waiv'':1284C ''weekend'':1219C ''wherea'':146C,201C,254C,295C ''whereof'':1382C ''whitcomb'':1418C,1421C ''wit'':1381C ''within'':1151C ''without'':405C ''work'':1092C,1114C,1167C ''write'':1290C ''written'':1201C,1342C ''§12.5'':1135C,1215C ''§5'':928C ''“agreement”'':71C ''“cel”'':498C ''“certifi'':494C ''“company”'':108C ''“dis”'':396C ''“effect'':486C,624C ''“facility”'':186C,410C ''“interconnect'':125C ''“parti'':132C ''“party”'':128C ''“point'':425C ''“poi”'':429C ''“standards”'':450C ''“tariff”'':384C ''”'':133C', 'executed isa harkwell ridge interconnection service agreement alleniom utilities der program office 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha 612 555 0100 alleniom.com doc no isa harkwell ridge rev final date 07 03 2025 owner der program office contracts agreement no. isa harkwell ridge project harkwell ridge solar application no. pxa 2024 0117 this interconnection service agreement this “agreement” is entered into by and between alleniom utilities an investor owned electric utility organized under the laws of the state of alleron with principal offices at 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha ein 36 4820917 the “company” and hailbouy solar with offices at 2200 ridge point road suite 400 halston alleron 03ha the “interconnection customer” each “party” and collectively the “parties.” this agreement is effective as of the date last executed below recitals whereas the interconnection customer filed with the company an application for interconnection service designated pxa 2024 0117 on 06 17 2024 in respect of 2.2 mw single axis tracker ground mount photovoltaic generating facility known as harkwell ridge solar the “facility” to be interconnected to the company distribution system at point on feeder aln 042 whereas the company completed technical screening system impact and facilities studies for the facility in accordance with the alleniom der interconnection standard dis 01 rev and issued final study determination approving the facility for execution of an interconnection service agreement at the capacity and point of interconnection described in the application as filed whereas the company tariff as filed with and approved by the alleron public utilities commission governs the interconnection of distributed energy resources of the facility class and forms an integral part of the terms and conditions of interconnection service provided hereunder whereas the parties intend by this agreement to establish the terms conditions rights and obligations under which the facility will be permitted to parallel with and export energy to the company distribution system now therefore in consideration of the mutual covenants and undertakings set forth herein and other good and valuable consideration the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged the parties agree as follows article definitions 1.1 capitalized terms not defined in this agreement shall have the meanings ascribed to them in the company filed tariff the “tariff” and in the alleniom der interconnection standard dis 01 rev the “dis” 1.2 for the purposes of this agreement and without limitation of the foregoing “facility” means the generating equipment ancillary equipment and all interconnection facilities described in article hereof “point of interconnection” or “poi” means the physical point at which the facility is electrically connected to the company distribution system as identified in article “standards” means the standards and specifications identified in article each as in effect on the effective date and as such may be amended superseded or reissued by the company in accordance with its ordinary regulatory practice “effective date” has the meaning given in article “certified equipment list” or “cel” means the company then current certified equipment list published by standards engineering article description of facility 2.1 project designation harkwell ridge solar application pxa 2024 0117 2.2 interconnection customer hailbouy solar 2.3 facility technology photovoltaic generation single axis tracker ground mount configuration 2.4 nameplate export capacity 2.2 mw ac at the point of interconnection 2.5 point of interconnection poi three phase primary tap on feeder aln 042 at the pole fkdn54d 2.6 point of common coupling pcc coincident with the point of interconnection identified in section 2.5 2.7 material terms the capacity technology and point of interconnection stated in this article are material terms of this agreement article term and effective date 3.1 effective date this agreement is effective as of 07 03 2025 the “effective date” being the date on which the last of the two parties has executed this agreement 3.2 term this agreement shall remain in full force and effect from the effective date until terminated in accordance with its terms or superseded by successor agreement between the parties 3.3 continuing obligations the obligations of the parties in respect of indemnity limitation of liability confidentiality and dispute resolution shall survive any termination or expiration of this agreement article interconnection standards 4.1 governing standards the facility shall at all times be designed constructed commissioned operated and maintained in conformity with the following company standards and any successor or superseding editions thereof dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard effective 03 01 2024 dps 07 rev distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 tcs 02 telemetry and communications standard effective 06 01 2021 and cel 2025 q2 certified equipment list published 04 30 2025 as such may be superseded from time to time 4.2 order of precedence in the event of any inconsistency among the documents constituting this agreement the following order of precedence shall govern the tariff ii the applicable company standards enumerated in section 4.1 iii the body of this agreement 4.3 compliance with successor standards nothing in this agreement shall be construed to relieve the interconnection customer from the obligation to conform the facility to successor or superseding editions of the standards as and when they take effect in accordance with the transition provisions of the applicable standard article metering and telemetry 5.1 metering revenue quality metering shall be provided at the point of interconnection in accordance with the tariff and the company metering specifications meters shall be owned installed tested and maintained by the company at the interconnection customer cost and shall be sealed at all times 5.2 telemetry in accordance with tcs 02 §5 the interconnection customer shall install at its cost provisions for utility owned remote terminal unit rtu and shall make available all analog and binary status dnp3 points required by the company telemetry and communications standard together with such communication paths and standing power provisions as the company requires for scada integration 5.3 commissioning of monitoring and control satisfactory commissioning and continuous availability of the telemetry described in section 5.2 are conditions precedent to permission to operate the facility shall not be paralleled with the company distribution system in the absence of live utility telemetry and any loss of telemetry after permission to operate shall be reported and remediated as provided in tcs 02 5.4 data and access rights the interconnection customer grants the company such rights of access to the facility and such rights to receive and use metering and telemetry data as are necessary for the company to discharge its obligations under the tariff and applicable standards article payment terms 6.1 construction work order the interconnection customer shall pay the company for the construction of upgrades and interconnection facilities in accordance with the construction work order issued under this agreement on the schedule and in the amounts set forth therein and in accordance with tariff §12.5 6.2 invoicing invoices shall be issued by the company and shall be due and payable within thirty 30 calendar days of the invoice date unless otherwise expressly provided in the construction work order amounts not paid when due shall bear interest at the rate set forth in the tariff 6.3 payment default in the event of non payment the company shall provide the interconnection customer written notice and payment deadline of thirty 30 business days in accordance with tariff §12.5 business days exclude weekends and federal holidays during the pendency of any such deadline the facility shall remain subject to any construction or commissioning hold ordered by the company 6.4 ongoing operational charges all charges credits and settlements applicable to interconnection service and associated ancillary services shall be as set forth in the tariff article amendments 7.1 amendments generally no term of this agreement may be modified or waived except by an instrument in writing signed by authorized representatives of both parties 7.2 governing standard post execution matters affecting material terms of article are governed by the company then current der interconnection standard 7.3 ministerial corrections corrections of clerical typographical or other manifest errors that do not affect material term of article may be made by written acknowledgment signed by authorized representatives of both parties 7.4 reservation nothing in this article shall limit the company right or obligation to require conformance of the facility to successor standards as provided in section 4.3 article signatures in witness whereof the parties have caused this agreement to be executed by their duly authorized representatives as of the dates set forth below this agreement being effective as of the date last executed alleniom utilities by dana whitcomb name dana whitcomb title vice president distribution operations date signed 07 03 2025 hailbouy solar by corey lindqvist name corey lindqvist title project director date signed 07 03 2025 executed in two counterparts each of which shall be deemed an original and both of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument filed with the der program office contracts alleniom utilities');
