''readi'':344C ''reason'':446C,592C,607C,695C ''receipt'':973C ''recogn'':857C ''ref'':48C ''regard'':102C,961C ''releas'':624C ''relev'':274C ''remain'':496C,840C,979C ''repeat'':131C ''repres'':231C,731C ''request'':243C,557C,679C,714C ''requir'':424C,448C,541C,622C ''resolv'':845C ''resourc'':124C,621C,790C,1019C ''respect'':556C,1002C ''respons'':613C,677C,682C ''restor'':884C ''review'':251C,427C ''risk'':403C ''save'':206C,376C ''scale'':113C,190C ''schedul'':738C ''scheme'':439C ''school'':23B,46C,75C,181C,303C,387C,469C,476C,480C,484C,705C,959C ''senior'':722C ''serious'':950C ''servic'':832C,903C ''sever'':146C,211C,910C ''share'':880C ''shift'':528C ''short'':765C ''silenc'':527C ''size'':290C ''solar'':27B,114C,191C ''specif'':606C ''specul'':284C ''spirit'':550C ''staff'':137C,817C ''stall'':26B,118C ''stand'':342C ''state'':185C,213C ''status'':534C,568C ''step'':801C ''street'':511C ''strong'':842C ''studi'':436C,664C ''submit'':1003C ''substanti'':824C ''suit'':1038C ''superintend'':1031C ''suspend'':497C,601C ''system'':364C,423C ''taken'':799C ''technic'':426C,447C ''telemetri'':670C ''telephon'':990C ''territori'':833C ''test'':668C ''thank'':993C ''time'':157C,430C ''timelin'':888C ''togeth'':658C ''town'':44C,486C,493C ''transpar'':886C ''treatment'':308C ''tresbay'':488C ''undersign'':688C ''understand'':412C,948C ''unifi'':468C ''unit'':39C ''unreason'':109C ''upon'':242C ''urgenc'':700C ''util'':64C,562C,786C,851C,860C,1023C ''utilities’'':121C ''veldmer'':522C ''vice'':59C ''view'':108C ''voic'':40C ''voter'':198C ''wastewat'':307C ''water'':305C ''whitcomb'':58C,79C ''whose'':188C ''will'':443C ''wit'':667C ''within'':119C,694C,834C ''without'':535C ''would'':963C ''write'':94C,174C,684C ''written'':676C', '2025 06 20 aml escalation letter alleron municipal league the united voice of alleron’s cities towns and school districts ref aml 2025 0620 der june 20 2025 ms dana whitcomb vice president distribution operations alleniom utilities re escalation der interconnection program delays affecting fourteen municipalities and school districts dear ms whitcomb on behalf of the alleron municipal league and the fourteen member communities identified below write to convey our formal and collective concern regarding the continued and in our view unreasonable delays affecting commercial scale solar interconnection projects currently stalled within alleniom utilities’ distributed energy resource der interconnection program this letter follows repeated informal outreach by individual member staff to your der program office over the preceding several months outreach which has not produced the clarity or the timely progress our members need in order to close out their local capital projects the league is writing on behalf of 14 municipalities and school districts across the state of alleron whose commercial scale solar projects commissioned in good faith with voter approved bond proceeds adopted capital budgets energy savings performance contracts and in several instances state and federal grant awards additional league members with projects in the same posture have asked to be represented collectively through this correspondence and are prepared to be identified upon request every one of these projects has been reviewed and approved by the applicable local governing body financed through public procurement and constructed by licensed contractors under permits issued by the relevant authority having jurisdiction the projects at issue are not speculative or exploratory they range in size from approximately 500 kw to nearly mw and are installed at public schools municipal water and wastewater treatment plants community centers public libraries and other municipal facilities in the great majority of cases construction is complete mechanical and electrical inspections have been closed out by local inspectors and equipment has been standing energized ready in some instances for period now measured in months pending only the company’s authorization to interconnect and place the systems into commercial operation each additional month of delay defers budgeted operating savings extends the payback horizon presented to our members’ councils and school boards and in the case of grant funded projects places committed public funding at direct risk of forfeiture our members are patient partners they understand that the interconnection of distributed generation on the company’s distribution system requires careful technical review and at times coordination with equipment procurement feeder studies and protection scheme confirmation they are willing to meet reasonable technical requirements what they are not able to accept and what this league cannot accept on their behalf is an brookfen unified school district city of elmsworth darnwick community school district lockmere community school district cravenwood community school district town of tresbay city of marden falls town of holcott remain suspended in your interconnection queue awaiting energization among the affected members are 812 larchmont street cordwyn alleron 16cw 651 555 0244 halston alleron 01ha 4200 veldmere boulevard extended period of silence shifting explanations and open ended hold status without clear articulation of what is required by whom and by when accordingly and in spirit of continued cooperation the league respectfully requests the following from alleniom utilities full accounting of current queue status for each identified league member project please provide the project’s assigned application number current queue position and complete processing history to date hold reasons for every project currently in hold pending or suspended posture please identify the specific reason for the hold the party responsible for the next action the information or resource required to release the hold and the date the hold was established expected energization dates for each project please provide the company’s current best estimate of the date on which permission to operate will be issued together with any intermediate milestone dates studies equipment delivery witness testing or telemetry acceptance that inform that estimate written response we request the company’s response in writing addressed to the undersigned at the league’s cordwyn office within reasonable period consistent with the urgency our members’ councils and school boards are attaching to this matter meeting we request an in person meeting between the company’s senior distribution leadership the league’s executive office and designated representatives of the affected members to be scheduled at the company’s offices in halston or at mutually convenient location in cordwyn at the company’s preference the league is prepared to convene our members on short notice once the company proposes date for your awareness copy of this letter has been provided to the alleron public utilities commission apuc energy resources division for the division’s information the league has taken this step not as matter of confrontation but out of good faith obligation to keep the commission’s staff apprised of program level concern affecting substantial number of alleron public entities across multiple service territories within the company’s distribution footprint it remains our strong preference to resolve this matter directly with alleniom utilities the league and its members recognize that alleniom utilities has been constructive counterparty on many prior initiatives and we approach this escalation with the expectation that the company shares our interest in restoring predictable transparent processing timelines to the der program our members’ communities have invested public funds published expected in service dates to their constituents and in several cases entered into contractual arrangements predicated on interconnection occurring by dates that are now past the credibility of local government energy planning across alleron is meaningfully bound up in the outcome and we are confident the company understands the seriousness with which we our elected officials and our school boards regard it would be grateful for the courtesy of an acknowledgment of receipt at your earliest convenience and remain available to discuss any aspect of the foregoing at the telephone number above thank you for your prompt attention to this matter respectfully submitted alden pryce alden pryce executive director alleron municipal league cc ms nia fairweather director energy resources division alleron public utilities commission apuc one league member managers and superintendents distribution list on file capitol plaza suite 900 cordwyn alleron 14cw');
