80C ''regard'':848C ''regulatori'':740C ''repli'':770C,775C ''request'':518C,670C,705C,730C ''requir'':789C ''resolv'':843C ''resourc'':808C ''respons'':119C ''return'':628C ''risk'':454C ''rosa'':24C,849C ''rosa.camarena'':26C,866C ''rtu'':248C,574C ''save'':353C,391C ''say'':756C ''school'':14B,42C,106C,143C,316C,326C,365C,422C,449C,623C,855C ''second'':77C,459C,640C ''semest'':460C ''senior'':736C ''serv'':103C,301C ''set'':489C ''short'':200C ''side'':136C ''sign'':480C ''signific'':343C ''silenc'':784C ''sit'':385C ''site'':266C,280C,288C,298C,545C,599C,674C ''slip'':456C ''solar'':101C ''somewher'':261C ''specif'':541C ''staff'':578C,811C ''stand'':173C,207C,514C ''status'':133C ''strength'':347C ''strong'':840C ''structur'':428C ''student'':331C,430C ''subject'':40C ''substitut'':525C ''superintend'':321C ''supplier'':256C ''support'':663C ''system'':170C,203C,384C,424C,659C ''talk'':834C ''taxpay'':411C ''telemetri'':244C,575C ''tell'':307C,683C ''ten'':180C ''term'':444C ''thereaft'':201C ''third'':79C,642C ''thirteen'':498C ''time'':80C,229C,766C ''today'':693C ''told'':238C ''track'':816C ''treat'':699C ''two'':100C,127C,544C,592C,673C ''under'':417C ''understand'':813C ''unifi'':105C,854C ''unit'':245C,576C,604C ''unmistak'':546C ''urgent'':41C ''us'':291C ''usd'':9B,503C ''use'':711C ''util'':95C,587C ''various'':241C ''wait'':593C,638C ''want'':64C ''week'':125C,168C,181C,381C,388C,634C ''weigh'':713C ''west'':183C,615C ''whatev'':707C ''whitcomb'':48C,723C ''whose'':810C ''without'':645C ''would'':116C,767C,831C,839C ''write'':61C,274C,764C ''written'':118C,704C,769C,774C ''year'':327C,350C,366C,450C ''yet'':251C', '2025 06 30 brookfen escalation from rosa camarena rosa.camarena brookfenusd.org to der.program alleniom.com date mon 30 jun 2025 09 42 18 0500 subject urgent school array energization priority cc dana whitcomb dana.whitcomb alleniom.com harriet ngoyi harriet.ngoyi alleniom.com to the der program office am writing again and want to be direct about the fact that this is not the first second or third time have raised this with your office to ask for firm answer on when alleniom utilities intends to energize the two solar arrays serving brookfen unified school district this message is dated 06 30 2025 and would like written response before the end of next week the two arrays in question and their status on our side are as follows brookfen north high school array 720 kw construction was declared complete by our contractor on 04 18 2025 the local electrical inspector closed out the installation the same week the system has been standing idle energized ready for more than ten weeks brookfen west elementary array 640 kw construction was declared complete on 05 23 2025 inspection was closed out shortly thereafter this system has now been standing idle for over month neither array has been energized neither array has firm energization date on record with the district each time our office contacts your program inbox we are told that component variously described as telemetry unit or an rtu has not yet been delivered by your supplier and that we are somewhere in queue behind other sites what we have never been given in writing is the position of our sites in that queue the identity of the sites ahead of us or the basis on which those sites are being served ahead of ours have to tell you plainly that the patience of the brookfen school board and the district superintendent is exhausted the 2025–2026 school year begins for our students on 08 26 2025 both of these arrays were financed in significant part on the strength of first year operating cost savings that were built into the district adopted budget for that same school year and presented to our board and to the community at public meetings every additional week that these systems sit dark is week of budgeted savings the district will not realize and will have to explain to the board to our parents and to the taxpayers of brookfen who approved the underlying bond measure our high school building systems curriculum was also structured around students being able to observe the array in operation from the beginning of the term that piece of the school year is now at risk of slipping into the second semester or being cut altogether you will by now have received the alleron municipal league letter of 06 20 2025 signed by executive director alden pryce escalating this same set of concerns on behalf of the district and thirteen other league members brookfen usd is one of the members named in that letter and stands fully behind the requests it contains this message is not substitute for the league letter it is intended to make the district individual position and the specifics of our two sites unmistakable to your office what am asking for directly is this in the next allocation of the equipment your program office is holding up as the constraint the rtu telemetry units your staff have referenced in prior calls am asking alleniom utilities to advance the district two waiting arrays ahead of the other sites presently competing for those units brookfen north completed construction on 04 18 2025 and brookfen west on 05 23 2025 both are public school facilities both have children returning to the building in eight weeks neither array can wait for second or third delivery cycle without meaningful harm to the district fiscal position and to the educational program these systems were installed to support if there is formal process for requesting that our two sites be advanced in your next equipment allocation please tell me what that process is and will follow it today if there is not please treat this message as our written request under whatever mechanism your program uses to weigh these decisions and please confirm receipt am copying ms whitcomb and ms ngoyi so that this request is on the record with senior distribution operations and regulatory affairs and so that no one at your program office is later in position to say the district did not put this in writing in time would like written reply not call back written reply by close of business friday 07 11 2025 silence past that date will require the district to raise this matter again through the league and if necessary directly with the commission energy resources division whose staff we understand is already tracking this program am available at 612 448 0311 during district business hours if it would help to talk any of this through would strongly prefer to resolve it with your office regards rosa camarena facilities director brookfen unified school district 1725 grantway drive brookfen alleron 12br 612 448 0311 rosa.camarena brookfenusd.org');
