616C,652C,778C,850C,916C,1028C ''requir'':427C,697C ''resourc'':33C,78C,133C,426C,1050C ''respons'':315C,418C,582C,592C,595C,782C,805C,826C,856C,869C,1042C ''restor'':1009C ''review'':847C ''rtu'':705C ''scale'':130C ''schedul'':214C,764C ''school'':119C,152C ''scope'':276C,293C,1021C ''screen'':718C ''sent'':576C ''separ'':329C ''servic'':169C,580C ''simplifi'':285C ''sincer'':1043C ''site'':354C ''small'':286C ''specif'':409C,957C ''staf'':765C ''stage'':990C ''standard'':402C,714C ''status'':176C,344C,405C,710C ''step'':361C ''studi'':364C,451C,465C,767C ''suffici'':723C,734C,833C ''suit'':373C ''summar'':330C ''summari'':17B,647C,656C,677C ''support'':759C ''suspend'':404C ''system'':142C,287C ''take'':952C ''tariff'':196C,461C,509C,587C,936C ''territori'':170C ''time'':484C,692C,769C,781C,902C,1024C ''timelin'':182C,454C,478C ''togeth'':345C,406C,475C,523C,569C,1003C ''total'':332C ''twelv'':517C,563C ''unambigu'':819C ''under'':641C,949C ''undersign'':791C ''understand'':639C ''upon'':729C ''util'':30C,57C,63C,84C,140C,260C,694C,766C,1054C,1065C ''veldmer'':386C ''view'':942C ''volum'':683C ''wastewat'':156C ''water'':154C ''week'':312C ''welcom'':774C ''whether'':500C ''withdraw'':511C,530C,547C ''withdrawn'':499C,597C ''within'':166C,185C ''workbook'':813C ''write'':787C,884C ''written'':502C,553C,655C ''≥500'':273C', '2025 07 07 apuc information request alleron public utilities commission energy resources division docket apuc 2025 er 014 ref erd ir 2025 07 014 date 07 07 2025 ms harriet ngoyi director regulatory affairs alleniom utilities re apuc information request alleniom utilities der interconnection program backlog docket apuc 2025 er 014 dear ms ngoyi the energy resources division of the alleron public utilities commission apuc is in receipt of correspondence from the alleron municipal league dated 06 20 2025 aml ref aml 2025 0620 der copied to the division escalating on behalf of fourteen member municipalities and school districts program level concern with the current pace of commercial scale distributed energy resource der interconnection processing on the alleniom utilities distribution system the league letter identifies delays affecting projects at public schools municipal water and wastewater facilities community centers and public libraries across multiple communities within the company service territory and raises questions regarding queue status hold posture and expected energization timelines that fall within the division continuing oversight of the company apuc filed interconnection tariff the division intends to be in position to brief the commission on the matter at the previously scheduled der program briefing on 09 10 2025 in advance of that briefing and to permit the division to assess the company der interconnection program on the basis of the company own records rather than the league characterization this letter requests the following information from alleniom utilities commercial der queue accounting for the commercial der interconnection program i.e. the ≥500 kw program scope portfolio administered by the company der program office simplified small systems process filings are outside the scope of this request the company is requested to provide complete queue accounting as of the most recent full week preceding the response date including at minimum the following presented at the individual application level and separately summarized in totals the count and identity of all applications currently in active processing status together with each application assigned application number applicant name site nameplate capacity filing date current processing step and the study or decision milestone next due one capitol plaza suite 900 cordwyn alleron 14cw 651 555 0180 apuc.alleron.gov halston alleron 01ha 4200 veldmere boulevard the count and identity of all applications currently on on hold pending customer pending standards or suspended status together with the specific hold reason of record for each the party responsible for the next action the information or resource required to release the hold and the date the hold was established the count and identity of all applications for which one or more study or processing timelines established under the company filed interconnection tariff procedures or executed study agreements have been exceeded as of the reporting date together with the timeline of record the actual elapsed time and the current cause of the overrun the count and identity of all applications withdrawn whether by written applicant request by application of the tariff deemed withdrawal provision or otherwise during the twelve months preceding the reporting date together with the effective date of each withdrawal and the recorded basis for it the count and identity of all formal notices of impending withdrawal notices of cancellation or equivalent written notices issued by the company to applicants during the twelve months preceding the reporting date together with the notice date the date sent the method of service the response deadline computed under the tariff and the current disposition response received no response deemed withdrawn other where any of the foregoing counts is materially affected by data integrity items known to the company requested to identify those items and provide the counts both as they presently appear in the company queue records and as the company understands the underlying facts to be backlog cause summary the company is further requested to provide written summary describing in the company own characterization the principal causes of the current backlog in the commercial der interconnection program the summary should address at minimum application volume relative to processing capacity the availability and lead time of utility owned equipment required for energization including but not limited to rtu and protection equipment the status of any internal standards reconciliation activity affecting screening or protection determinations the sufficiency of certified equipment references relied upon by the company the sufficiency of hosting capacity information made available to prospective applicants and any other factors the company identifies as materially contributing to the current queue posture supporting quantitative material equipment delivery schedules staffing utilization study cycle times and the like is welcome and where practicable requested format and timing responses should be provided in writing addressed to the undersigned at the division cordwyn office with electronic copies to the docket line item responses under item above may be provided by workbook attachment provided each attachment is unambiguously cross referenced to the corresponding item responses should be received by the division sufficiently in advance of the 09 10 2025 briefing to allow the division adequate review the division requests that the company provide its response no later than 08 22 2025 and where any portion of the response cannot be furnished by that date that the company so advise the division in writing no later than 08 08 2025 with an explanation and proposed alternative date continuing dialogue for example timing differences reconciliation items or other known data quality issues the company is this request is issued in the ordinary course of the division monitoring of interconnection program performance under the company apuc filed tariff the division has no present view as to the merits of the underlying matter and takes no position on the specific project level concerns raised in the league 06 20 2025 letter which remain properly matter between the league member entities and the company in the first instance the division interest at this stage is limited to the queue accounting and backlog cause information described above together with the company plan for restoring predictable processing to the program the division remains available to discuss scope format or timing questions at company request the division appreciates the company continued cooperation and looks forward to the company response sincerely nia fairweather nia fairweather director energy resources division alleron public utilities commission nia.fairweather apuc.alleron.gov 651 555 0180 cc commissioners alleron public utilities commission docket file apuc 2025 er 014 mr alden pryce executive director alleron municipal league for the division information consistent with the league 06 20 2025 correspondence enclosures none');
