:208C,397C ''solar'':407C ''stand'':533C ''state'':315C ''statement'':112C ''status'':107C ''step'':353C ''studi'':263C,375C ''subject'':62C,92C ''submiss'':87C ''submit'':72C,121C,543C ''submitt'':180C ''substat'':95C,161C,239C ''suit'':147C ''target'':111C ''technolog'':105C ''telephon'':80C ''time'':204C ''topolog'':421C ''type'':103C ''updat'':371C ''upgrad'':473C ''util'':46C,128C,192C,572C ''welcom'':387C ''wish'':230C ''within'':158C ''work'':405C ''would'':311C,318C,355C,386C,480C ''written'':320C,449C', '2025 07 02 preapp request aln 108 northline renewables llc pre application request feeder capacity confirmation date july 2025 to alleniom utilities der program office der.program alleniom.com from peter ashford director of project development northline renewables llc subject pre application request mw project on feeder aln 108 submitting party developer applicant business address primary contact telephone email request details field date of submission addressed to program inbox subject requested feeder substation area requested project capacity der category interconnection type anticipated technology site status anticipated in service target statement of request northline renewables llc is pleased to submit this pre application request to alleniom utilities for feeder capacity confirmation in advance of formal application we are developing mw pure generation 1840 ferngate parkway suite 210 halston alleron 02ha 612 555 1826 photovoltaic project sited within the elderpine substation service area and have identified feeder aln 108 as the intended point of interconnection in preparation for this submittal we have reviewed the feeder hosting capacity map published by alleniom utilities distribution planning which was the current published edition available at the time of our project sizing decisions per the published hosting capacity map dated 05 15 2024 feeder aln 108 shows 3.0 mw of available capacity we wish to proceed with mw project at the elderpine substation service area and request confirmation the published map lists aln 108 as pure generation feeder segment at 13.2 kv with the last planning study reflected as 04 2024 our proposed project is fully aligned with the der category shown for the feeder project capacity has been scoped at nameplate 3.0 mw so as to sit at rather than above the published available figure with the express intent of avoiding request that would exceed the feeder stated headroom we would appreciate written confirmation from the der program office that the 3.0 mw published availability on feeder aln 108 remains current as of the date of this request and guidance on the pre application dialogue steps alleniom would like to conduct prior to our filing of formal interconnection application should distribution planning have updated feeder figures or study results that post date the 05 15 2024 publication we would welcome the opportunity to receive that information so we can size the project accordingly additional information project name working elderpine solar nameplate dc approximately 3.9 mw dc nameplate ac interconnection request mw ac inverter topology central inverters with plant level scada compatible controller export profile 100 export no on site load environmental permitting interconnection critical path permitting proceeding in parallel requested response written confirmation of currently available capacity on feeder aln 108 for pure generation interconnection at the requested mw nameplate any known conditions restrictions or upgrade indications identified by distribution planning that would apply to mw project at this location scheduling of pre application dialogue meeting with distribution planning and the der program office at alleniom earliest convenience northline renewables llc appreciates the der program office consideration of this pre application request we remain available at the contact information above for any clarifying questions and stand ready to provide additional project detail as required respectfully submitted peter ashford peter ashford director of project development northline renewables llc peter.ashford northlinerenewables.com 612 555 1826 date signed 07 02 2025 enclosure reference feeder hosting capacity map alleniom utilities distribution planning publication dated 05 15 2024');
