C,1157C,1321C,1331C ''§3.6'':167C,292C,500C,839C,1334C,2032C,2044C,2172C,2279C ''§4'':1787C ''§5'':302C,1842C,2259C ''§6'':2201C ''§7'':178C,328C,2313C ''§8'':2617C ''≥500'':563C,2075C', 'dis 01 rev4 der interconnection standard dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page alleniom utilities der interconnection standard doc no rev effective date owner dis 01 rev 03 01 2024 alleniom standards engineering evan solberg document control item value document number dis 01 revision rev effective date 03 01 2024 supersedes dis 01 rev 12 01 2021 basis ieee 1547 2018 owner alleniom standards engineering evan solberg approved by manager standards engineering distribution alleniom der program office interconnection studies der planning group scada ems engineering regulatory affairs contracted developers on request next scheduled review 03 01 2027 revision history rev date summary rev 06 01 2016 initial issue rev 09 01 2018 alignment with ieee 1547 2018 introduced category protective equipment table rev 12 01 2021 program scope threshold set at 500 kw added §3.4 aggregation rev 03 01 2024 added §3.5 shared poi eligibility added §3.6 controlled capacity recognition ul 1741 ul 3141 pcs control narrative §7 restated to require withdrawal and reapplication for post execution capacity or poi changes table rewritten by category §1 purpose and scope this standard establishes the technical and procedural requirements for interconnection of distributed energy resources der to the alleniom utilities distribution system it is based on ieee 1547 2018 and applicable state interconnection rules filed with the alleron public utilities commission apuc and it applies to all der classes defined in §3 dis 01 rev governs classification of der facilities by aggregate nameplate capacity at the point of common coupling §3 eligibility to share an existing point of interconnection where legacy equipment is on site §3.5 recognition of controlled operating limit below nameplate §3.6 protective and control equipment requirements by class and category §5 dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 treatment of post execution changes to executed interconnection service agreements §7 this standard is read together with the apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 where topic is addressed by both this standard and the tariff the tariff controls requirements for real time monitoring and communications integration are established under tcs 02 and are not restated here except by cross reference §2 references the following documents are referenced within this standard unless otherwise noted the latest published revision applies ieee 1547 2018 ieee standard for interconnection and interoperability of distributed energy resources with associated electric power systems interfaces dps 07 rev alleniom distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 establishes distribution protection requirements including protective devices at points of interconnection with export capable in scope facilities tcs 02 alleniom telemetry communications standard effective 06 01 2021 governs utility owned rtu installation and scada telemetry for der at and above the program scope threshold establishes the condition for permission to operate cel 2025 q2 alleniom certified equipment list published 04 30 2025 listing basis ul 1741 sb and ul 3141 the cel front matter restates §3.6 of this standard erp alleniom engineering referral procedure form er 11 §3 routes any standards §3 der classification der facilities are classified by aggregate nameplate capacity at the point of common coupling in accordance with ieee 1547 2018 class thresholds applicable review path and equipment references are stated in table commercial small scale 500 kw–1 mw medium scale mw–5 mw program scope ≥500 kw sub 500 kw der commercial and residential is handled under the simplified small systems process outside the der program definitions of terms used in this standard follow ieee 1547 2018 and where applicable the definitions in the apuc filed tariff the terms aggregate nameplate capacity and point of common coupling pcc have the meanings assigned by ieee 1547 2018 and reflected in company practice the terms point of interconnection poi export capable and pure generation site are used in accordance with their ordinary meaning in utility interconnection practice dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 table der classes class aggregate nameplate at pcc program status review path protective equipment reference residential small commercial 500 kw simplified small systems process outside the der program simplified small systems screening table category commercial small scale 500 kw mw in der program scope initial screening supplemental review under srp table category medium scale mw mw in der program scope initial screening system impact study table category large scale out of scope for this standard mw handled under transmissio interconnection procedures full study process not addressed the program scope threshold is 500 kw facilities below 500 kw whether commercial or residential in customer class are routed to the simplified small systems process and are not administered by the der program §3.1 determination of aggregate nameplate capacity aggregate nameplate capacity is the sum of the manufacturer rated ac output ratings of all generating equipment interconnected or proposed to be interconnected at single point of common coupling manufacturer datasheets govern derated or operating figures do not substitute for nameplate except as provided in §3.6 §3.2 point of common coupling the point of common coupling is the point at which the der facility is electrically connected to the company distribution system as further defined in ieee 1547 2018 the pcc is distinct from the point of interconnection poi the latter being the physical demarcation of company owned protective and metering equipment §3.3 determination on the basis of application classification is determined on the facility as filed and as physically configured on site filing captions project titles and cover letter characterizations do not alter classification the connection diagram the equipment schedule and the address of record govern §3.4 aggregation co located der behind the same point of common coupling counts toward one site total previously interconnected legacy equipment counts toward the aggregate regardless of the vintage of its permission to operate regardless of whether it predates any current alleniom standard and regardless of the sequence or form in which subsequent applications are submitted at the same pcc the aggregate governs the facility class and the resulting program scope determination an applicant proposing new der at premises that already hosts der shall identify the existing equipment on the application form and shall submit one line diagram showing the electrical relationship of the proposed equipment the existing equipment the customer load the customer meter and the pcc interconnection studies verifies against the company existing der register §3.5 shared poi eligibility new der may share an existing poi only where the combined facility including legacy equipment can be brought to current monitoring control standards otherwise separate poi and new application are required where the existing system operates behind the meter new der may instead be interconnected front of the meter under its own service and poi and is then evaluated on its own capacity without aggregation dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 the two dispositions available under §3.5 are shared poi aggregated the combined facility legacy equipment plus proposed equipment is brought to current monitoring control standards as prescribed by tcs 02 and by table at the aggregate class the applicant is responsible for the retrofit and for demonstrating retrofit feasibility to interconnection studies where feasibility is confirmed the application proceeds at the aggregate capacity at the shared poi separate poi non aggregated front of the meter alternative where the existing system operates behind the meter and the applicant elects to interconnect the new der front of the meter under separate service and its own poi the new der is evaluated on its own capacity without aggregation with the legacy equipment class placement review path and table category are determined from the new der capacity alone retrofit feasibility of legacy equipment is factual question the company will not decide from records alone the applicant or its authorized developer must confirm feasibility in writing absent that confirmation the shared poi path under §3.5 is not available and the application is redirected to §3.5 or withdrawn §3.6 controlled capacity recognition limit below nameplate is recognized only with valid ul 1741 ul 3141 pcs certification plus an approved control narrative sufficient in themselves for recognition where the site arrangement includes utility equipment the recognized limit is enforced as applicable telemetry monitoring and on pure generation sites the poi recloser ansi 32 directional power element set to the recognized limit and tripping on violation required submissions to have controlled operating limit recognized in place of aggregate nameplate for program scope and study purposes the applicant shall submit both of the following valid power control system pcs certification issued under ul 1741 including supplement sb where applicable and or ul 3141 identifying the specific equipment arrangement at the applicant site and the setpoint range an approved control narrative written engineering document describing how the site control system enforces the requested operating limit including the sensed quantities the response actions the response times the interlocks and any allowable modes and their setpoint ceilings these two documents taken together are sufficient in themselves to establish recognition of the controlled limit recognition establishes the capacity at which the facility is reviewed classified and studied enforcement backstops as arrangement provides where the site arrangement includes utility equipment the recognized limit is enforced by the arrangement existing equipment as follows telemetry monitoring for sites at or above the tcs 02 threshold the company rtu to scada telemetry monitors real power export at the point of interconnection against the recognized limit sustained deviation triggers investigation under tcs 02 and may result in hold on permission to operate poi recloser directional power element pure generation sites on pure generation sites sites at which no customer load is served behind the point of common coupling where utility poi recloser is installed per table and dps 07 the recloser ansi 32 directional power element is set to the recognized limit and trips the site on violation the ansi 32 element is inherently available in modern reclosers and does not require additional utility hardware enforcement provisions apply only as the site arrangement provides them their absence at particular site does not reopen the recognition determination once the two required submissions are on file no controlled limit without submissions in the absence of both valid ul 1741 ul 3141 pcs certification and an approved control narrative nameplate governs for classification program scope determination and study certified equipment list cel 2025 q2 restates this section in its front matter listing of pcs on the current cel does not by itself constitute recognition of controlled limit for particular site the applicant site specific certification and control narrative are always required dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 §4 screening and study process applications in der program scope proceed through initial technical screening under interconnection studies facilities not passing initial screens may be evaluated under supplemental review per srp or advance to system impact study this standard does not restate srp the daytime minimum load convention and other screen methodologies are prescribed there §5 protective and control equipment protective equipment requirements are stated by category in table keyed to the classes of §3 table protective equipment by category item category 500 kw category 500 kw mw export sites category mw mw export sites applicable class residential small commercial commercial small scale medium scale der side disconnect required customer owned lockable visible break required customer owned lockable visible break required customer owned lockable visible break interconnection protective functions ieee 1547 2018 clause provided by certified inverterprovided by certified inverter and or dedicated protection relay dedicated protection relay required der breaker with protection relay scheme for load generation decoupling arrangements not required as specified per site by protection engineering as specified per site by protection engineering poi recloser utility owned not required category export sites poi recloser not required required anti islanding certified inverter functions per ieee 1547 2018 certified inverter functions per ieee 1547 2018 supplemented by relay scheme where dedicated relay is installed dedicated relay scheme with transfer trip where required by protection engineering directional power element ansi 32 pure generation sites not applicable set on poi recloser where installed used to enforce §3.6 controlled limit where applicable set on poi recloser used to enforce §3.6 controlled limit where applicable metering bidirectional revenue meterbidirectional revenue meterbidirectional revenue meter primary or secondary as feeder configuration requires utility rtu and scada telemetry not required required per tcs 02 ≥500 kw required per tcs 02 notes to table category placement reflects the export configuration prevailing at the site where site configuration warrants requirements differing from the tabular default including for example load generation decoupling arrangements in which generation is isolated by der breaker with dedicated protection relay scheme protection engineering may specify the applicable requirements through the engineering referral procedure erp §3 form er 11 dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 table addresses protective and control equipment monitoring and communications requirements are established under tcs 02 where §3.6 recognition is in effect at pure generation site with utility poi recloser the ansi 32 directional power element is set to the recognized limit and trips on violation §6 monitoring and control facilities at or above the tcs 02 program threshold shall provide real time monitoring and control integration through utility owned rtu with scada telemetry as prescribed by tcs 02 live telemetry to the company system operations center is condition of permission to operate this standard does not restate tcs 02 refer to tcs 02 §5 for the telemetry rule and to alleniom system operations for rtu installation scheduling site level control functions required by §3.6 power control system recognition by table dedicated protection relay schemes der breaker arrangements and by erp site determinations together satisfy the control integration expectations of this section as applied to the specific facility §7 capacity and point of interconnection provisions post execution changes to executed isa capacity or poi require withdrawal and reapplication isa edits are not permitted for capacity or poi changes scope this section governs changes proposed after an interconnection service agreement has been executed by both parties prior to execution ordinary revisions may be handled in the studies and drafting process without invoking this section principal parameters facility capacity and point of interconnection are principal parameters of the interconnection service agreement studies protective equipment scoping and queue position each depend on these parameters as executed required path customer or developer seeking to change either the executed capacity or the executed point of interconnection after isa execution shall submit written request to withdraw the current application and terminate the executed isa file new application at the desired capacity and where applicable the desired point of interconnection and accept the new queue position corresponding to the filing date of the new application the new application is studied on its own facts the withdrawal and reapplication path applies whether the requested change is an increase or decrease in capacity and whether or not the requested change is characterized by the applicant as involving new or existing equipment other post execution changes modifications to protective schemes telemetry endpoints equipment models within the same nameplate rating and administrative items that do not alter capacity or poi are handled under the change order provisions of the executed isa and are not subject to this section downstream effects the withdrawal of an executed isa under this section releases any related utility equipment reservations and any related feeder headroom allocations which are then available to subsequent applications in queue order studies previously performed at the withdrawn capacity are not carried forward the new application receives new study appropriate to its filed parameters §8 records and compliance interconnection studies retains the application file executed isa and study record for each in scope facility for the retention period established by regulatory affairs standards engineering maintains the current revision of this standard the certified equipment list cel 2025 q2 and subsequent editions and the engineering referral procedure erp register of per site determinations dis 01 rev alleniom der interconnection standard page dis 01 rev effective 03 01 2024 any conflict between this standard and the apuc filed tariff is resolved in favor of the tariff any conflict between this standard and another alleniom operating standard encountered in screening or study is referred to per site engineering determination under erp §3 end of dis 01 rev');
