ject'':432C,1449C ''submers'':389C ''substitut'':1001C ''suffici'':442C ''supersed'':61C ''supervis'':1300C,1345C,1631C ''suppli'':632C ''synchron'':761C,1184C,1567C ''system'':98C,105C,258C,273C,304C,364C,455C,485C,516C,694C,768C,830C,1090C,1190C,1281C,1594C,1622C,1693C ''tcs'':412C,832C,1328C,1563C ''telemetri'':414C ''termin'':659C ''territori'':217C ''test'':1437C,1453C,1458C,1468C,1506C,1523C,1543C,1634C,1654C,1671C,1683C ''time'':506C,536C,749C,1062C,1201C,1256C,1536C ''transfer'':1267C,1270C ''transform'':398C,628C,959C,1014C,1513C,1516C ''transit'':945C ''trip'':505C,573C,1061C,1261C,1268C,1271C,1542C ''unaccept'':1286C ''underfrequ'':757C ''undervoltag'':752C ''unintent'':110C ''unless'':862C ''unnecessari'':572C ''upon'':456C,486C ''upstream'':544C,1135C,1162C,1310C,1337C,1407C ''use'':775C ''util'':36C,96C,123C,215C,411C,418C,460C,467C,496C,515C,562C,568C,593C,642C,828C,897C,902C,923C,935C,989C,1078C,1153C,1174C,1189C,1473C,1500C,1610C,1621C,1643C,1667C,1677C ''vault'':387C ''verif'':1521C,1552C,1565C,1573C ''verifi'':1179C ''via'':826C ''visibl'':126C,519C,880C,892C,1575C ''voltag'':490C,627C,695C,1080C,1515C ''warrant'':1380C ''week'':943C ''wit'':1497C ''within'':212C,503C,1253C ''without'':571C,944C,1231C,1433C ''withstand'':1505C ''would'':471C ''write'':868C,1420C,1607C ''written'':1434C ''zone'':1066C,1289C ''§4'':296C ''§4.2'':1008C ''§5'':803C ''§6.2'':1600C', 'dps 07 rev2 distribution protection standard dps 07 rev distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 page alleniom utilities standards engineering distribution protection standard doc no rev date owner dps 07 rev 09 15 2023 alleniom standards engineering effective date 09 15 2023 supersedes dps 07 rev 11 04 2019 classification engineering standard distribution protection approved by manager standards engineering purpose dps 07 establishes minimum protection requirements for the interconnection of distributed energy resources der to the alleniom utilities distribution system the requirements set forth herein preserve system side fault clearing prevent unintentional islanding of generation onto de energized distribution circuits and ensure that the utility maintains controllable visible interruption point at every generating facility capable of exporting power to the distribution network this standard defines the equipment functional performance and coordination principles applicable to protective devices installed at the point of interconnection poi of an export capable der site it is issued by standards engineering under authority of the director of distribution engineering and shall be applied to all in scope projects at initial screening detailed engineering review construction and commissioning scope this standard applies to all distribution connected export capable der sites within the alleniom utilities service territory including but not limited to commercial small scale der 500 kw mw nameplate medium scale der mw mw nameplate any der of any size that is capable by facility design or operating configuration of exporting real power to the distribution system through the point of common coupling sub scope der handled under the simplified small systems process are outside the direct application of this standard however where such facility is nonetheless configured for export the protection principles of §4 shall apply as adapted by the small systems review non export configurations facilities operated behind reverse power lockout with no export capability under any operating condition are outside the scope of this standard and are addressed under separate protection guidance references the following documents are referenced in the application of this standard ieee 1547 standard for interconnection and interoperability of distributed energy resources with associated electric power systems interfaces ieee c37.230 guide for protective relay applications to distribution lines ieee c37.60 iec 62271 111 requirements for overhead pad mounted dry vault and submersible automatic circuit reclosers ansi c57.13 requirements for instrument transformers dps 07 rev distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 page alleniom utilities tcs 02 telemetry communications standard alleniom utilities erp engineering referral procedure protection requirements 4.1 general every distribution connected der site subject to this standard shall be equipped with protective equipment sufficient to accomplish at minimum the following isolate the der from the distribution system upon loss of the utility source before the operation of any utility reclosing sequence that would attempt to re energize the affected circuit isolate the der from the distribution system upon detection of abnormal voltage or frequency conditions on the utility side of the point of interconnection within the trip times required by the applicable interconnection standard present the utility system operator with visible remotely operable and lockable point of interruption between the der and the distribution circuit at all times when the der is connected coordinate with upstream and downstream distribution protective devices such that der side fault is cleared by der side devices and utility side fault is cleared by utility side devices without unnecessary tripping of either 4.2 point of interconnection recloser requirement every export capable in scope der site shall be equipped with utility owned point of interconnection poi recloser no exceptions are specified the poi recloser shall satisfy the following requirements ownership and control the poi recloser and its associated control cabinet communications interface current and voltage transformers and control power supply shall be owned installed maintained and operated by alleniom utilities the der owner shall provide the physical site the equipment pad primary conductors to the recloser terminals and any auxiliary services grounding station service communications backhaul as specified in the site construction package ratings the recloser shall be rated for the maximum continuous current momentary current short circuit interrupting current and system voltage of the feeder or lateral to which it is connected with margin per distribution protection engineering feeder specific settings sheet functional elements at minimum the recloser control shall implement the following ansi device functions with settings determined per site by distribution protection engineering 50 51 phase and 50n 51n ground overcurrent instantaneous and time 27 59 undervoltage and overvoltage 81u 81o underfrequency and overfrequency 25 synchronism check for closing into an energized system 32 directional power element available for use as an export limit enforcement or reverse power backstop as directed by the site engineering determination 79 automatic reclosing enabled or blocked per the coordination scheme in §5 operability the recloser shall be capable of local manual operation local electrical operation from the control cabinet and remote operation and monitoring via the utility scada system per tcs 02 loss of communications shall not defeat local protection where referenced external standard is revised the revision in effect on the date of the site engineering determination shall govern unless standards engineering directs otherwise in writing dps 07 rev distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 page visible break and lockout the recloser shall provide or be paired with visible break disconnect operable by utility personnel with provision for utility padlocking in the open position for the purpose of clearance holds location the poi recloser shall be located on the utility side of the point of interconnection at location accessible to alleniom utilities crews 24 hours per day days per week without transiting locked customer premises 4.3 der side protection der side protection generator step up transformer protection inverter interface protection plant collection protection and any owner installed disconnects shall be provided by the der owner coordinated with the poi recloser settings and reviewed by alleniom utilities distribution protection engineering prior to commissioning der side protection does not substitute for the poi recloser required under §4.2 4.4 grounding the der interconnection transformer grounding configuration shall be determined per site to be compatible with the grounding of the connected distribution circuit in accordance with distribution protection engineering grounding practice memorandum for the affected feeder class 4.5 anti islanding the der shall be equipped with anti islanding protection meeting the trip times and non detection zone requirements of the applicable interconnection standard passive schemes based solely on utility side voltage and frequency measurement are permitted only where the site system impact study demonstrates the passive scheme detection performance for the range of expected islanding conditions on the connected feeder otherwise an active or communications assisted scheme shall be provided coordination requirements 5.1 coordination with feeder reclosing the poi recloser shall be coordinated with the upstream feeder recloser and any mid line reclosers such that the poi recloser opens on loss of the utility source before the first reclose attempt of any upstream recloser the poi recloser remains open and locked out until the utility source has been restored verified stable per the site synchronism check settings and the utility system operator has authorized reconnection per the site operating procedure coordination time current characteristics shall be documented in the site protection coordination study prior to energization 5.2 coordination with der side protection der side protective devices shall clear der side faults without operation of the poi recloser to the extent reasonably practicable where der side fault is not cleared by der side devices within the allowable time the poi recloser shall trip as backup protection 5.3 direct transfer trip direct transfer trip dtt shall be applied at any site where the system impact study identifies an unacceptable non detection zone for anti islanding or where the connected feeder configuration requires supervised opening of the poi recloser on operation of an upstream device where dtt is applied the associated communications channel shall meet the availability and monitoring requirements of tcs 02 5.4 reclosing blocking automatic reclosing on the upstream feeder recloser may be blocked delayed or supervised at sites where the der contribution to fault current the der anti islanding characteristic or the customer load composition on the dps 07 rev distribution protection standard effective 09 15 2023 page affected feeder warrants such change the determination shall be made per site by distribution protection 5.5 settings governance all protection settings for the poi recloser and any changes to upstream feeder recloser settings driven by the der interconnection shall be issued in writing by distribution protection engineering and shall not be altered in the field without written revision order testing 6.1 factory acceptance the poi recloser and its control shall be subjected to factory acceptance testing per the manufacturer standard test protocol and per ieee c37.60 iec 62271 111 with test records delivered to alleniom utilities prior to shipment 6.2 site acceptance prior to placing the der site in service the following site acceptance activities shall be performed and witnessed by alleniom utilities insulation resistance and dielectric withstand testing of primary and secondary circuits current transformer and voltage transformer ratio polarity and burden verification functional testing of each enabled ansi device function against its issued setting including pickup timing and reset end to end trip testing from each protection element through the recloser interrupter verification of local and remote scada control status and metering per tcs 02 verification of synchronism check and reclose block logic verification of visible break disconnect operation and lockout provisions 6.3 commissioning and cutover cutover of the der site to the distribution system shall not proceed until all §6.2 activities are complete and accepted in writing by alleniom utilities the site initial parallel operation shall be observed by the utility system operator with the poi recloser under active scada supervision 6.4 periodic testing the poi recloser shall be included in the utility periodic recloser maintenance program der side protective devices shall be tested by the der owner on schedule not to exceed that of comparable utility owned equipment with test records made available to alleniom utilities on request 6.5 post event testing following any operation of the poi recloser attributable to system disturbance der side event or mis operation distribution protection engineering shall review the event records and direct such retesting or resetting as it determines appropriate before the site is returned to service end of dps 07 rev distribution protection standard distribution alleniom standards engineering master file distribution protection engineering distribution operations der program office apuc filing informational engineering and recorded in the site interconnection file');
