r alleniom standards engineering approved by manager standards engineering distribution alleniom der program office interconnection studies distribution protection engineering scada ems engineering der planning group regulatory affairs attachments bulletin eb 2025 03 03 24 2025 form er 11 template precedent register revision history rev date summary rev 07 10 2022 initial issue established referral form and per site engineering determination path rev 03 24 2025 reissued in conjunction with bulletin eb 2025 03 §3 rewritten to state routing rule for standards conflicts form er 11 fields expanded to capture site type and feeder precedent register appended §1 purpose erp establishes the procedure by which an interconnection application encountering standards conflict silence between standards or site conditions falling outside the assumptions of tabulated requirement is referred to per site protection scada engineering determination the procedure exists so that documentary conflicts between alleniom standards do not accumulate as screening holds against active applications and so that each affected site is resolved on the merits of its own protection scheme on schedule stated in §4 this procedure is issued by standards engineering and applies uniformly across the alleniom der program it is read together with dis 01 der interconnection standard dps 07 distribution protection standard tcs 02 telemetry communications standard and the apuc filed interconnection tariff §2 scope erp applies to any in scope der application administered by the alleniom der program at which one or more of the following conditions is encountered during initial screening supplemental review or system impact study two applicable alleniom standards state requirements that cannot both be applied on their face to the affected site an applicable standard is silent as to site condition materially present in the application topic on which the standard does not speak as distinct from topic on which it speaks and permits an exception the reviewing engineer documents reasoned basis to depart from tabulated requirement in light of the site specific protection arrangement sub scope facilities handled under the simplified small systems process are outside the direct application of erp the small systems reviewer may nonetheless invoke form er 11 where an export configuration warrants site specific protection engineering input nothing in this procedure permits screening hold pending revision of standard where erp provides determination path see §3 and bulletin eb 2025 03 attached §3 referral routing any standards conflict encountered at screening or design shall be routed via form er 11 to per site protection scada engineering determination no “winning” document is selected across the program each site is resolved on its own protection scheme the reviewing engineer in interconnection studies initiates the referral by completing form er 11 template attached attaching the relevant excerpts of the standards at issue the application connection diagram and equipment schedule and any feeder specific information required to characterize the site protection arrangement interconnection studies transmits the completed form er 11 to distribution protection engineering where scada ems input is required the manager distribution protection engineering routes copy to the scada ems engineering group for concurrent review referral does not itself alter the application status in the der program queue the affected application remains in queue during the referral period and other screening activities that are not dependent on the referred question shall proceed in parallel the per site engineering determination is issued in writing on form er 11 by distribution protection engineering is signed by the responsible engineer and countersigned by the manager distribution protection engineering and is filed with the application record the determination is binding for the referred site and does not create general rule across the program subsequent site presenting similar question is referred and determined on its own facts where the site protection arrangement as determined under this section differs from the tabular default of dis 01 §5 table the engineering determination on form er 11 supplements the site protective equipment scoping and is provided to the der program office and to the contracts desk for incorporation into the interconnection service agreement where the referral resolves recurring pattern that standards engineering considers appropriate to reflect in future revision of standard the determinations are logged and reviewed as provided in §5 §4 timelines timelines below run from the date on which interconnection studies transmits the completed form er 11 to distribution protection engineering business days exclude weekends and federal holidays referral class description determination due class standards conflict no site protection novelty two alleniom standards state conflicting requirements at site whose protection arrangement is otherwise ordinary 10 business days class standards conflict with site protection novelty conflict at site whose arrangement e.g. load generation decoupling non standard grounding unusual feeder configuration requires additional protection engineering review 20 business days class standards silence site condition outside tabulated assumptions applicable standard is silent as to site condition materially present determination may require coordination study 30 business days class scada ems input required in addition to protection engineering any of the above where the site telemetry or control arrangement requires concurrent scada ems engineering review 30 business days classification is made by the manager distribution protection engineering on receipt of form er 11 where the reviewer requests reclassification the request is decided in writing within two business days extensions to the timelines above are permitted only