7 2025 alleniom distribution operations document control supersedes none initial issue review cycle annual or on material change to supplier lead times or operating criticality categories approving authority vp distribution operations distribution der program office interconnection studies der planning group system operations center soc standards engineering supply chain distribution equipment §1 scope this guideline governs deployment sequencing of constrained utility equipment rtus reclosers across completed sites awaiting energization it applies to alleniom owned devices installed by distribution operations for the purpose of energizing construction complete distributed energy resource der site when supplier lead times or quarterly delivery quantities constrain the number of sites that can be equipped in given deployment window this guideline does not apply to application processing nondiscriminatory queue order treatment of interconnection applications is governed by interconnection tariff §12.7 and by the procedures administered by interconnection studies nothing in this guideline modifies displaces or supplements those procedures the rankings established under §2 operate solely on sites for which interconnection application processing is complete the interconnection agreement where required is executed and construction is certified complete by the customer or its contractor devices out of scope customer owned protective equipment utility owned equipment already installed at the site distribution system reinforcement equipment scheduled under an approved capital work order program scope for the underlying der remains as defined in dis 01 rev §3 and interconnection tariff §12.2 §2 commissioning criticality 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha as general rule deployment priority for constrained equipment follows interconnection queue order consistent with the nondiscriminatory treatment principles of interconnection tariff §12.7 site may be advanced ahead of queue order under certain circumstances the urgent nature of request in particular for public infrastructure schools hospitals water wastewater facilities or an expedited deployment pathway on reasonable customer request but only where substantiated by the site own recorded attributes per §3 in order of priority essential service function water wastewater emergency health committed in service or grant funding deadline construction complete date among sites of the same critical nature the deciding factor is interconnection queue order requests not substantiated by these attributes remain in queue order og 17 rev equipment deployment prioritization guideline page factor definitions essential service function site whose primary served load is public water or wastewater facility hospital emergency response or first responder facility or public health facility for which loss of service is treated as an emergency by the responsible jurisdiction essential service status is evidenced by the customer facility classification of record and where applicable the served load designation on the interconnection application committed in service or grant funding deadline contractually committed in service date or date on which grant funding lapses if the site is not in service established in fully executed written instrument between the customer and governmental funder project sponsor or off taker internal customer construction targets marketing dates budget cycle expectations and school year fiscal year or seasonal preferences do not constitute committed deadline under this factor construction complete date the calendar date on which the customer construction of the site was certified complete and ready for utility energization steps where more than one date is recorded the earlier of the customer written notice of construction completion and the utility on site verification controls queue date as tiebreaker the interconnection queue date of the site underlying application used only to break tie among sites that rank equally on factors and external advocacy correspondence volume elected official inquiries and stakeholder communications received in relation to site do not enter the ranking ranking is determined from the raw attributes above evidenced by the source documents in §3 §3 documentation for each deployment window the der program office shall assemble deployment worksheet listing every site meeting the eligibility conditions of §1 with the following fields drawn from the identified system of record site name and interconnection application id der program queue customer party of record and site service address der program queue nameplate capacity and program scope classification per dis 01 rev §3 application file devices required to energize rtu poi recloser or both quantities and specification references standards engineering construction complete date and source of certification project construction file contracted in service or grant funding deadline if any with the executed instrument establishing it attached by reference customer submission essential service classification if any with the customer facility classification of record attached by reference application file interconnection queue date der program queue the worksheet shall record the §2 factor on which each ranked site qualifies sites that do not qualify at ranks or are ranked by with as tiebreaker the worksheet the ranked deployment list and the assigned equipment set identifiers shall be retained in the der program equipment planning file for the applicable window and provided to the soc concurrent with the coordination step described in §5 og 17 rev equipment deployment prioritization guideline page amendments to the worksheet arising after issuance for example receipt of previously missing documentation for listed site or arrival of new site into the waiting population shall be recorded in an addendum bearing its own date prior ranked lists are not overwritten §4 vendor engagement expectations distribution operations working through supply chain shall maintain rolling engagement with the current approved suppliers of rtus and poi reclosers with the following expectations lead time visibility monthly written statement of committed lead times next scheduled delivery date and delivery quantity per device type retained in the equipment planning file any change to previously committed date or quantity is to be flagged in writing on receipt order coverage standing purchase orders shall cover no fewer than the number of device sets required to satisfy the sites eligible under §1 for the current deployment window plus the next scheduled delivery window expedite requests shall be pursued where delivery date change would displace rank or rank site alternate sourcing where committed lead times exceed the interval between deliveries supply chain shall document the shortcoming of the current approved suppliers and evaluate qualification of additional vendors under standards engineering certification procedures qualification effort shall not condition or delay deployment decisions for the current window substitution any proposed substitution of device model or configuration relative to the site approved specification is routed to standards engineering substitutions are not accepted on schedule pressure alone escrow spares minimum spare quantity per device type shall be held at the operations warehouse replenished on drawdown and not consumed to accelerate lower ranked site ahead of higher ranked site whose device set is en route vendor engagement records are subject to audit by regulatory affairs on request §5 coordination with the system operations center the ranked deployment list issued under §3 is transmitted to the soc concurrent with its issuance coordination steps are as follows pre deployment briefing for each device set scheduled to arrive in the deployment window the der program office and the soc shift supervisor confirm the receiving site the anticipated field installation window the commissioning sequence and the telemetry integration steps required for permission to operate pto nothing in this guideline modifies the soc pto gating criteria tcs 02 §5 requires utility owned rtu and scada telemetry with live telemetry established prior to pto for sites at or above 500 kw and this guideline does not authorize interim or provisional energization ahead of that condition change control change to the ranked list after transmittal to the soc for example arrival of new rank site or documented lapse of committed deadline previously credited at rank is issued by written addendum jointly to supply chain and to the soc verbal reprioritization is not to be relied upon field constraints where feeder condition crew availability or outage window constraints prevent installation at higher ranked site within the window the soc records the constraint and the der program office reissues the deployment assignment for that device set to the next eligible site the og 17 rev equipment deployment prioritization guideline page higher ranked site retains its rank for the following window commissioning readiness the soc pto hold log continues to govern which completed sites are eligible for energization steps sites without established telemetry remain on the hold log until the utility owned rtu is installed and telemetry is verified in accordance with tcs 02 reporting written record of device set assignments installation dates commissioning outcomes and any addenda issued during the window is retained by the der program office and made available to regulatory affairs and to the soc on request end of guideline og 17');
