'§5'':909C ''§6'':426C,1090C,1098C ''§7'':323C ''≥500'':249C', 'srp rev3 supplemental review procedure srp rev supplemental review procedure effective 02 10 2025 alleniom utilities standards engineering page alleniom utilities standards engineering supplemental review procedure doc no rev effective date owner srp rev 02 10 2025 alleniom standards engineering supersedes srp rev effective 07 22 2022 classification technical standard distributed energy resource interconnection distribution der program office interconnection studies distribution planning standards engineering regulatory affairs §1 purpose this procedure defines the supplemental review process applied to distributed energy resource der interconnection applications that fail one or more of the fast track technical screens set out in the alleniom der interconnection standard dis 01 rev it establishes the ordered screens data sources and documentation to be produced by the interconnection engineer conducting supplemental review and identifies the conditions under which study agreement is required before the application may proceed supplemental review is intended to allow an application that fails an initial fast track screen to be evaluated against bounded set of additional technical criteria without incurring the cost and schedule of full system impact study where that evaluation can be completed from existing feeder data and standard engineering judgment nothing in this procedure alters the substantive interconnection standards contained in dis 01 the protection requirements contained in dps 07 or the telemetry and communications requirements contained in tcs 02 §2 scope this procedure applies to all in scope der interconnection applications ≥500 kw as defined in dis 01 §3 that have entered supplemental review following failure of an initial screen and all der classes recognized in dis 01 §3 commercial small scale 500 kw mw and medium scale mw mw this procedure does not apply to sub 500 kw installations processed under the simplified small systems process capacity or point of interconnection changes to an executed interconnection service agreement which are governed by dis 01 §7 or domestic rooftop solar which is out of scope for the der program where supplemental review screen result is inconclusive on the record before the engineer the application shall be advanced to study agreement rather than passed or failed under this procedure §3 screens srp rev supplemental review procedure effective 02 10 2025 alleniom utilities standards engineering page applications entering supplemental review shall be evaluated under the following screens in the order given an application that fails any screen shall be considered candidate for study agreement the reviewing engineer shall document the failing screen the underlying data and the recommended disposition per §6 screen aggregate der penetration on the feeder total nameplate der existing plus queued plus requested on the subject feeder shall not exceed the applicable penetration threshold set in dis 01 queue positions are those on record with the der program office at the date of screen evaluation screen voltage regulation and flicker reviewed against the feeder most recent planning study or where none is on file for the subject feeder within twenty four 24 months against screening voltage rise calculation performed using conductor and transformer impedance from the distribution planning record screen short circuit contribution der short circuit contribution shall not cause any feeder protective device to exceed 87.5 of its interrupting rating nor cause any downstream protection coordination margin to fall below the values specified in dps 07 screen 100 of minimum load screen for solar governed by §4 screen reverse power flow at substation where the aggregate der on the subject feeder exceeds the substation transformer certified reverse power capability or where reverse power protective settings are not in place the application shall be routed to study passing all applicable screens is necessary but not sufficient condition for interconnection the application remains subject to the balance of the dis 01 evaluation including protection and telemetry requirements §4 100 of minimum load screen for solar 100 of minimum load screen for solar for solar der the minimum load used in this screen shall be the minimum load within the daytime window 10 00–16 00 determined from feeder ami interval data the absolute overnight minimum shall not be used requested der capacity must be this daytime window minimum for the site to pass the screen the daytime window minimum shall be computed from feeder ami interval data covering the most recent complete twelve 12 calendar months aggregated to fifteen minute intervals aligned to the feeder ami collection cadence and evaluated only over intervals whose start time falls within 10 00–16 00 local clock time on the feeder intervals affected by known feeder outages load transfers or planned switching shall be excluded and the exclusion documented in the reviewer worksheet where fewer than twelve 12 months of ami interval data are available the reviewer shall use the longest continuous complete period available and note the data window length in the supplemental review memo the daytime window minimum determined under this section is the sole minimum load figure used for the solar 100 of minimum load screen feeder minimum load figures produced for other purposes planning studies hosting capacity map inputs protection coordination are not substitutes for the value computed under this section and shall not be carried into the screen determination without recomputation on the ami record where prior supplemental review memo on the same feeder has applied different minimum load basis the reviewer shall recompute the value under this section and if the two disagree supersede the earlier memo in the file §5 data sources the following data sources are authoritative for supplemental review under this procedure srp rev supplemental review procedure effective 02 10 2025 alleniom utilities standards engineeringpage feeder ami interval data from the alleniom ami data warehouse at the meter aggregation level published for the subject feeder ami interval data is the sole authoritative source for the screen minimum load determination described in §4 distribution planning record most recent feeder planning study conductor and transformer impedance data and protection coordination settings held by distribution planning der queue active queue and on hold registers maintained by the der program office as of the screen evaluation date queue entries not yet reflected in published hosting capacity map remain applicable to screen certified equipment list cel current edition for verification that proposed inverters and pcs equipment are eligible to be considered under the screens interconnection application record the applicant filed capacity single line diagram inverter specifications and control narrative where controlled capacity operation is asserted under dis 01 §3.6 substitution of source not listed above shall be documented in the memo produced under §6 together with the reason for the substitution §6 documentation the reviewing engineer shall produce supplemental review memo for each application processed under this procedure the memo shall contain at minimum application identifier applicant subject feeder and requested capacity the screens applied and the pass fail determination for each for screen the daytime window minimum load determined per §4 the data window used the count of intervals evaluated and any interval exclusions with reason the recommended disposition advance without study agreement advance to study agreement or return to applicant with specified deficiency reviewer signature and date and the identifiers of any earlier supplemental review memos superseded the memo shall be filed to the interconnection application record within five business days of screen completion where memo supersedes an earlier determination on the same application or the same feeder the superseded memo shall be flagged in the file and cross reference to the superseding memo added to its cover alleniom utilities der program office 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha 612 555 0100 alleniom.com');
