ndards engineering document title telemetry communications standard applies to distributed energy resource der facilities interconnected to the alleniom utilities distribution system within the der program scope effective date 06 01 2021 approving authority manager standards engineering §1 purpose this standard establishes the minimum technical and operational requirements for real time telemetry and communications between in scope distributed energy resource der facilities and the alleniom utilities system operations center soc it governs the equipment data content refresh cadence communications transport and cybersecurity posture required for der facility to be observed and dispatchable through the utility supervisory control and data acquisition scada system tcs 02 is one component of alleniom der interconnection framework its provisions are limited to telemetry and communications requirements for interconnection classification protective functions service agreements commissioning and other lifecycle activities are addressed in the standards and procedures cited by the interconnection standard dis 01 and are outside the scope of this document §2 scope tcs 02 applies to every in scope der site as defined by dis 01 §3 that is every der whose nameplate capacity meets or exceeds the der program threshold of 500 kw sub 500 kw der handled under the simplified small systems process is outside the scope of this standard tcs 02 applies to commercial small scale der 500 kw mw medium scale der mw mw aggregated der facilities recognized as single site under dis 01 §3.4 where the aggregate capacity meets or exceeds the der program threshold der commissioned on or after the effective date of this standard and der commissioned before the effective date that undergo material modification poi relocation or capacity change requiring new interconnection application 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha 612 555 0100 alleniom.com tcs 02 rev effective 06 01 2021alleniom utilities standards engineering page 2telemetry communications standard tcs 02 where der site interfaces with the distribution system through shared point of common coupling with other generation the aggregate facility is the object of this standard and the aggregate is measured and controlled as single interconnected entity §3 rtu requirements §3.1 ownership and installation each in scope der site shall be equipped with utility owned remote terminal unit rtu installed at or immediately adjacent to the point of interconnection the rtu shall be procured owned installed configured maintained and where required replaced by alleniom utilities the customer shall provide the physical mounting location environmental enclosure station ac service and communications entrance conduit specified in the utility site specific rtu installation drawing §3.3 functional requirements each rtu shall at minimum poll the der facility generation metering inverter pcs gateway and station instrumentation at the refresh cadence specified in §6 encode and forward the required data points §6 to the alleniom scada front end processors over an approved communications path §4 timestamp all values to common reference §3.5 and buffer data locally for minimum of seventy two 72 hours in the event of communications loss with automatic backfill upon restoration report communications status device health and configuration version to scada as diagnostic points accept authenticated remote configuration updates and firmware from alleniom scada ems engineering only §3.4 environmental and station service requirements the rtu enclosure shall meet the environmental rating specified in the site specific installation drawing station ac service to the enclosure shall be provided by the customer through dedicated branch circuit backed by an uninterruptible supply sized for minimum four hour outage ride through sufficient to maintain telemetry through short duration station outages §3.5 time synchronization the rtu shall discipline its internal clock to an authoritative time source using either gnss gps time or the alleniom scada network time reference all values reported to scada shall carry timestamp accurate to within ±1 second of utc §3.6 commissioning and end to end verification §3.2 approved models the utility owned rtu shall be one of the three models currently used for utility owned rtu service yot 8963 yot 8856 or yot 7963 substitution is not permitted customer power plant controller ppc may use any rtu on the plant side provided it can communicate with the utility owned rtu via dnp3 §4.2 tcs 02 rev effective 06 01 2021 alleniom utilities standards engineering page telemetry communications standard tcs 02 prior to the rtu being accepted as commissioned alleniom shall perform an end to end point to point test that verifies each required data point §6 at the scada operator display exercises any control points released to scada and validates alarm and quality flags commissioning of the rtu is prerequisite to the telemetry condition stated in §5 §4 communications §4.1 communications transport the rtu shall communicate with alleniom scada over one of the transports approved by scada ems engineering utility managed fiber to an alleniom aggregation node or utility provisioned licensed private wireless point to multipoint or utility provisioned cellular service on the approved carrier list using sim credentials held by alleniom customer owned or shared use networks are not permitted as the primary telemetry transport where site conditions do not permit any of the transports listed above the site is not eligible for interconnection under the der program until suitable transport can be provisioned §4.2 scada protocol the rtu shall communicate with scada using dnp3 serial or dnp3 over tcp ip secure authentication v5 shall be enabled on the dnp3 link where supported by the rtu configuration parameters dnp3 addresses timeouts unsolicited response classes integrity poll intervals shall follow the site specific configuration record issued by scada ems engineering §4.3 availability the end to end telemetry path rtu transport front end processor shall be designed for monthly availability of not less than 99.5 percent measured at the scada front end persistent loss of telemetry constitutes departure from the site interconnection basis and shall be corrected by the customer and utility working together to the extent each owns the affected equipment §4.4 address and ip management all ip addresses dnp3 addresses vlan assignments and routing between the rtu and alleniom scada are assigned and managed by alleniom customer equipment shall not initiate connections toward the rtu other than as expressly permitted in the site specific configuration record §5 telemetry condition for permission to operate §5 ≥500 kw requires utility owned rtu scada telemetry no pto without live telemetry this requirement applies to all in scope der sites including aggregated facilities under dis 01 §3.4 live telemetry for the purposes of §5 means that the rtu installed under §3 is physically installed configured and end to end commissioned in accordance with §3.6 tcs 02 rev effective 06 01 2021 alleniom utilities standards engineering page telemetry communications standard tcs 02 communicating with alleniom scada over an approved transport §4 at the refresh cadence required by §6 and presenting all required data points §6 as valid not stale not forced not flagged bad quality at the scada operator display at the moment permission to operate pto is issued compliance with §5 is confirmed by the soc shift supervisor on shift at the time pto is requested the soc confirmation is recorded against the interconnection file pto shall not be issued to any in scope der site until §5 is satisfied §6 data points and refresh rates §6.1 required data points each in scope der site shall present at minimum the following analog and status points to alleniom scada where the site arrangement includes multiple inverter blocks or multiple aggregated facilities behind common poi values shall be reported both individually per block and as facility total analog values per site and per block where applicable point units sign convention real power net export at poi kw export positive reactive power net at poi kvar absorbing positive poi voltage per phase poi current per phase frequency at poi hz gross generation per inverter block kw generation positive auxiliary parasitic load where separately metered kw load positive cumulative energy delivered kwh export positive cumulative energy received kwh import positive ambient cabinet temperature rtu health °c status and diagnostic points point description site online offline aggregate operating state of the der inverter pcs block status per block run standby fault communications heartbeat rtu to scada path health time sync quality gnss ntp discipline status configuration version active rtu configuration identifier alarm summary rolled up device alarm state §6.2 refresh rates tcs 02 rev effective 06 01 2021 alleniom utilities standards engineering page telemetry communications standard tcs 02 analog values shall be updated to scada at intervals no longer than four seconds using dnp3 class event reporting for point on change and class integrity poll no less frequently than every sixty 60 seconds status points shall be reported by exception on change of state with an integrity poll no less frequently than every sixty 60 seconds cumulative energy registers shall be reported no less frequently than every five minutes §6.3 data quality every value delivered to scada shall carry dnp3 quality flag values shall be marked online restart communications lost or over range as circumstances warrant values held constant by the rtu during communications loss shall not be reported as online upon restoration they shall be reported with the communications lost flag until fresh source values are acquired §6.4 retention alleniom retains all telemetry from in scope der sites in the historian for minimum of thirty six 36 months at the raw acquisition cadence and indefinitely at hourly aggregation for planning engineering analysis and regulatory reporting §7 cybersecurity §7.1 applicability the rtu the communications transport between the rtu and alleniom scada and any customer equipment that shares physical or logical interface with the rtu are subject to this section alleniom owned assets covered here are administered under alleniom cyber security program consistent with nist sp 800 82 and nerc cip where applicable §7.2 access control local and remote access to the rtu is limited to alleniom scada ems engineering and to alleniom authorized service personnel local craft access requires two factor authentication against alleniom identity system passwords shared secrets and cryptographic keys are managed by alleniom and are not disclosed to the customer developer or any third party §7.3 communications security dnp3 secure authentication v5 shall be enabled where supported by the rtu all communications traversing any non utility segment shall be tunneled through an alleniom managed vpn using ipsec ikev2 with mutual certificate authentication certificates shall have maximum validity of thirteen 13 months and are rotated by alleniom §7.4 firmware configuration and change management rtu firmware and configuration are updated only by alleniom scada ems engineering following the alleniom change management process firmware images shall be verified against cryptographic signature prior to installation the customer shall not attempt to modify upgrade or reconfigure the rtu or the utility owned communications equipment §7.5 logging and monitoring the rtu shall log authentication events configuration changes communications state transitions and firmware operations logs are forwarded to alleniom centralized log management system anomalies detected by that system are handled per alleniom cyber security incident response procedure tcs 02 rev effective 06 01 2021 alleniom utilities standards engineering page telemetry communications standard tcs 02 §7.6 physical security the rtu shall be housed in locked tamper evident enclosure enclosure keys cores and any physical access tokens are held by alleniom physical intrusion of the enclosure shall generate status point tamper alarm reported to scada under §6 §7.7 incident response the customer shall report without delay any known or suspected compromise of the rtu its enclosure its communications transport or any interface between customer equipment and utility owned telemetry equipment reports shall be directed to the alleniom soc and to scada ems engineering §7.8 decommissioning at end of life the rtu and its cryptographic material are returned to alleniom for secure disposal customer equipment previously interfaced to the rtu shall be sanitized of any alleniom provided credentials before it is repurposed or disposed of end of tcs 02');
