C,257C', 'tariff excerpt s12 interconnection apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection provisions filed with the alleron public utilities commission electric tariff volume iii original sheet no 214 effective march 2024 section 12 interconnection of distributed energy resources §12.1 applicability this section governs the interconnection to alleniom utilities the “company” distribution system of distributed energy resources “der” within the alleron service territory technical requirements screens study procedures and equipment standards referenced herein are set out in the company der interconnection standard dis 01 and companion standards each of which is incorporated by reference nothing in this section shall be construed to modify or supersede any applicable safety reliability or protection requirement of the company engineering standards filed by alleniom utilities 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection volume iii sheet no 214 apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of §12.2 scope of the der interconnection program the der interconnection program administered under this section applies to applications for der interconnection at or above five hundred kilowatts ≥500 kw within the program der shall be classified according to the der interconnection standard as follows commercial small scale der five hundred kilowatts to one megawatt 500 kw mw medium scale der one megawatt to five megawatts mw mw the program scope threshold is ≥500 kw der below five hundred kilowatts sub 500 kw whether commercial or residential are not administered under this section and shall instead be processed under the company simplified small systems process which is filed separately and is outside the der interconnection program aggregation controlled capacity recognition and shared point of interconnection eligibility are addressed in the der interconnection standard and shall control the classification of any facility whose nameplate rating aggregate site rating or point of common coupling brings it within program scope alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection volume iii sheet no 214 apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of §12.3 application intake and queue position complete application shall establish the applicant queue position as of the date the company determines the application to be complete applications determined to be incomplete shall be returned with written deficiency notice identifying each item requiring cure and the date by which cure is required queue position is not transferable between applications except as expressly provided in the der interconnection standard §12.4 deemed withdrawal following notice of impending withdrawal or cancellation upon issuance of formal written notice of impending withdrawal cancellation by the company the applicant shall have thirty 30 business days from the date of the notice to submit substantive response curing the matter identified therein if the applicant fails to respond within thirty 30 business days the application shall be deemed withdrawn and shall be closed from the active queue without further action of the company for purposes of this section “business days” shall exclude saturdays sundays and federal legal public holidays observed within the response window without limitation the following federal holidays falling within response windows relevant to the current filing period are recognized as non business days and shall not be counted holiday observed date memorial day 05 26 2025 juneteenth national independence day 06 19 2025 independence day 07 04 2025 the notice of impending withdrawal cancellation shall be served in writing certified mail or verified electronic delivery and shall state the date of issuance the response deadline computed under this section and the consequence of non response the company shall maintain log of all notices issued dates of service and dispositions alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection volume iii sheet no 214 apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of §12.5 construction payment defaults where construction work order or interconnection facilities invoice becomes payable and the customer has not remitted the amount due the company shall inform the customer in writing of the outstanding balance and shall issue payment deadline of thirty 30 business days from the date of that written notice for so long as the thirty 30 business day payment deadline is running the affected project shall remain on hold in the queue and shall not be deemed withdrawn the construction payment default procedure under this §12.5 is distinct from and shall not be conflated with the deemed withdrawal procedure under §12.4 the two mechanisms have different triggers different consequences and different cure paths upon receipt of full payment prior to expiration of the deadline the company shall promptly release the hold and resume the affected work in queue order if the deadline expires without payment the company may pursue such remedies as are available under the applicable interconnection service agreement and this tariff including as separate and subsequent step issuance of notice of impending withdrawal cancellation under §12.4 alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection volume iii sheet no 214 apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of §12.6 interconnection service agreement interconnection service shall commence only upon execution of an interconnection service agreement “isa” and the company written permission to operate material terms of an executed isa including but not limited to nameplate facility capacity and the designated point of interconnection may not be modified by amendment post execution changes to such material terms require withdrawal of the affected application and re application in accordance with the der interconnection standard §12.7 nondiscriminatory queue order processing of applications applications shall be processed by the company in queue order on nondiscriminatory basis no applicant shall be advanced or disadvantaged in the processing sequence by reason of identity affiliation customer class geography or any other factor not expressly provided for in this tariff or in the der interconnection standard scope note this §12.7 applies to application processing only that is to the sequencing of screening technical review study assignment and issuance of interconnection determinations utility construction sequencing and the scheduling and allocation of constrained utility owned equipment including without limitation remote terminal units point of interconnection reclosers and other supply limited devices are not governed by this section such matters are addressed under the company operating guidelines including og 17 equipment deployment prioritization guideline which sets forth the criticality factors and prioritization criteria applicable to constrained equipment nothing in this §12.7 shall be construed to require the company to sequence construction or equipment deployment in queue order where og 17 or another operating guideline provides different criticality based ordering alleniom utilities apuc filed interconnection tariff §12 interconnection volume iii sheet no 214 apuc tariff filing alleniom utilities electric tariff vol iii §12 page of §12.8 reservation the company reserves the right to seek modification of this section through filing with the alleron public utilities commission nothing in this tariff limits any authority reserved to the commission by statute rule or order issued by director regulatory affairs alleniom utilities filed pursuant to order of the alleron public utilities commission docket sheet reference apuc alleniom utilities electric tariff volume iii §12 interconnection provisions');
