:159C,188C,356C,1062C ''take'':414C,1129C ''target'':774C,875C ''tcs'':133C,1103C ''telemetri'':130C,1106C ''test'':2A,9B,20C,40C,69C,90C,228C,236C,243C,276C,518C,653C,660C,692C,754C,757C,765C,796C,812C,816C,835C,856C,867C,886C,910C,953C,987C,992C,1003C,1018C,1041C,1077C ''time'':383C,499C ''trip'':811C ''unlist'':372C ''upon'':1028C ''use'':678C ''util'':28C,34C,64C,456C,475C,793C,980C ''valu'':998C ''veldmer'':461C ''verif'':821C ''verifi'':562C ''waiv'':93C,223C ''waiver'':3A,10B,21C,41C,119C,239C,244C,261C,294C,328C,408C,487C,511C,582C,654C,723C,747C,957C,964C,1081C ''wit'':1A,8B,19C,39C,67C,89C,227C,242C,275C,517C,652C,659C,753C,756C,794C,849C,866C,885C,909C,986C,990C,1007C,1076C ''withdraw'':376C ''without'':881C ''witness-test'':7B ''written'':721C,961C ''§1'':57C ''§2'':145C ''§3'':238C ''§4'':519C ''§4.1'':521C,1085C ''§4.2'':697C,748C ''§4.3'':860C,911C ''§6'':827C ''“supersedes”'':554C ''“waiver'':317C,713C,949C ''“wit'':691C,952C', 'witness test waiver procedure eng prc 014 rev alleniom utilities der program office page alleniom utilities der program office der witness test waiver procedure doc no eng prc 014 rev 04 30 2025 owner standards engineering evan solberg §1 purpose this procedure establishes when alleniom utilities personnel must witness commissioning tests of customer’s distributed energy resource der prior to issuance of permission to operate pto and when the on site witness test may be waived on the basis of the equipment installed at the facility it is the controlling document for the der program commissioning group and for standards engineering waiver dispositions companion documents alleniom der interconnection standard dis 01 rev telemetry communications standard tcs 02 the current edition of the alleniom certified equipment list cel §2 scope applies to every in scope der facility interconnecting to the alleniom distribution system under the der program commercial small scale 500 kw mw and medium scale mw mw domestic rooftop der and sub 500 kw facilities routed through the simplified small systems process are outside the scope of this procedure applies to the initial commissioning of new interconnection to re commissioning following capacity change or protective equipment replacement and to the disposition of any request to waive the on site witness test in favor of an accepted commissioning agent test record §3 waiver eligibility rule witness test waivers apply only to equipment listed on the current edition of the certified equipment list at the waiver date equipment not carried on the current cel edition requires an on site witness test before permission to operate pto is issued listings appearing solely on superseded cel edition do not confer waiver eligibility on the current edition date the following are corollaries of the rule and are provided for the avoidance of doubt the “waiver date” is the date on which standards engineering signs the waiver disposition not the date on which the applicant filed the interconnection application executed the isa or completed construction every protective device and every inverter or power conversion system installed at the facility must appear on the current cel edition facility with any single unlisted component is ineligible withdrawal of an equipment listing at the time of cel republication is substantive event listing that was carried on prior edition and was not carried forward into the successor edition confers no waiver eligibility once the successor edition takes effect front matter footnotes cross references or historical annotations in the current cel that describe prior edition’s contents are informational only they do not extend eligibility to models that are not themselves listed in the body of the current edition alleniom utilities der program office 4200 veldmere boulevard halston alleron 01ha 612 555 0100 alleniom.com eng prc 014 rev alleniom utilities der program office page the cel edition in force on the waiver date is the sole reference model that was listed at the time an application was filed but is no longer listed on the waiver date requires the on site witness test §4 procedure §4.1 look up model against current cel the commissioning coordinator retrieves the current edition of the certified equipment list from the standards engineering document repository the coordinator confirms the edition identifier and the “supersedes” reference on the cel cover page and verifies that no more recent edition has been published between the file date shown on the coordinator’s copy and the waiver disposition date for each inverter and each protective device installed at the facility the coordinator locates the exact make model and firmware family in the body of the current cel and records the cel row reference on the commissioning checklist if any installed model is not present in the body of the current cel including any model that appears solely on superseded cel edition the facility is ineligible for witness test waiver and an on site witness test is required prior to pto superseded editions of the cel are archived and are not to be used to establish eligibility under this section the coordinator marks the commissioning checklist “witness test required” and forwards to §4.2 where every installed model is confirmed on the current cel the coordinator marks the checklist “waiver eligible” and forwards to standards engineering for written disposition waiver disposition remains at the discretion of standards engineering positive eligibility determination under this section is necessary but not sufficient condition for issuance of waiver §4.2 schedule an on site witness test where witness test is required the commissioning coordinator schedules the test with the customer or the customer’s commissioning agent targeting the earliest mutually available date consistent with the applicant’s construction complete status and the availability of an alleniom utilities witness engineer testing shall be performed per ieee 1547.1 and shall include at minimum the protective function trip tests the anti islanding test and the ride through verifications specified in dis 01 rev §6 the customer or commissioning agent supplies the test plan calibrated instrumentation and the qualified personnel to operate the equipment the alleniom witness engineer observes records and dispositions the test in accordance with §4.3 where the required on site witness test cannot be scheduled prior to the applicant’s targeted energization date the facility remains without pto on site witness testing is not to be deferred to post pto date under any circumstance and pto is not to be issued conditionally against future witness test §4.3 documentation the commissioning coordinator maintains single commissioning record for each facility the record shall include at minimum the completed commissioning checklist including the cel edition identifier consulted the cel row reference for each listed model and the “waiver eligible” or “witness test required” determination for waiver eligible facilities the written standards engineering waiver disposition signed and dated by the standards engineer of record eng prc 014 rev alleniom utilities der program office page for witness tested facilities the witness engineer’s test record including instrument identifiers measured values pass fail dispositions per test point and the witness engineer’s signature and date the manufacturer’s certificate of conformance factory test report or equivalent evidence supporting the cel listing relied upon correspondence with the customer or commissioning agent bearing on scheduling deferrals or test plan negotiation the commissioning record is retained in the facility interconnection file and is prerequisite to pto issuance by the system operations center pto shall not be issued in the absence of either signed witness test disposition or signed waiver disposition supported by §4.1 eligibility determination against the current cel edition end of procedure see dis 01 rev for interconnection standards tcs 02 for telemetry requirements and the current cel edition for the list of qualifying equipment revisions to this procedure are issued by standards engineering and take effect on the date shown in the document control block above');
