lendar 2024 weekday daytime 10 00 to 16 00 410 to 620 kw weekend daytime 170 to 260 kw annual peak 744 kw 08 14 2024 15 00 assumptions export at the point of interconnection was studied at 860 kw with zero park load the bounding case for voltage rise and reverse power flow fault contribution was taken at 1.1 per unit of inverter rated current anti islanding is by the inverters ul 1741 sb active scheme all six models are carried on cel 2025 q2 results screen result basis steady state voltage at poi full export light load 1.031 pu limit 1.05 pu dis 01 rev voltage change on loss of full output 2.1 percent limit percent dis 01 rev thermal loading aln 088 trunk 71 percent of rating at full export feeder model 2025 01 fault current contribution at poi 41 three phase 1.1 pu inverter current islanding non detection zone not identified dtt not required dps 07 §4.5 §5.3 conditions of interconnection 4.1 utility owned poi recloser per dps 07 §4.2 with settings issued by distribution protection engineering under dps 07 §5.5 automatic reclosing at the poi recloser to be blocked with the recloser locked out on loss of the utility source per dps 07 §5.1 synchronism check 25 to supervise closing 4.2 upstream feeder recloser aln 088 r2 first reclose interval raised from 0.5 to 2.0 so the poi recloser opens on loss of source before the first reclose attempt dps 07 §5.1 4.3 directional power element 32 at the poi recloser applied as an export backstop at 900 kw 2.0 4.4 utility owned rtu and scada telemetry per tcs 02 including the §6.1 points ahead of permission to operate tcs 02 §5 4.5 protection coordination study and sign off by distribution protection engineering before energization dps 07 §5.1 status study complete 06 22 2025 conditions 4.1 4.3 and 4.5 pass to distribution protection engineering 4.2 to distribution operations 4.4 to scada ems engineering devon reyes der planning group 06 22 2025');
